506
00:28:31,209 --> 00:28:34,170
<i>'cause we didn't have money enough</i>
<i>to get a hotel room,</i>

507
00:28:34,254 --> 00:28:38,091
{\an8}<i>to being on </i>TRL
<i>and people screaming in Times Square</i>

508
00:28:38,174 --> 00:28:39,884
{\an8}<i>when we would walk to the windows.</i>
<i>It was insane.</i>

509
00:28:41,553 --> 00:28:42,637
<i>♪ Say it ain't so... ♪</i>

510
00:28:42,721 --> 00:28:44,389
[Tom] <i>Shit was just, like, exploding.</i>

511
00:28:45,140 --> 00:28:46,766
That was quite a wild ride.

512
00:28:46,850 --> 00:28:47,976
<i>♪ Carry me home ♪</i>

513
00:28:48,059 --> 00:28:51,438
<i>♪ Na-na, na-na, na-na, na-na, na-na... ♪</i>

514
00:28:51,521 --> 00:28:53,440
[Travis]
<i>We were three kids just trying to navigate</i>

515
00:28:53,523 --> 00:28:55,900
<i>through this new world together.</i>

516
00:28:56,943 --> 00:28:58,528
<i>But there was a sense of comfort</i>

517
00:28:58,611 --> 00:29:01,197
<i>because I was doing it</i>
<i>with, like, my two brothers.</i>

518
00:29:01,281 --> 00:29:05,034
<i>♪♪</i>

519
00:29:05,118 --> 00:29:08,163
[crowd cheering]

520
00:29:15,712 --> 00:29:19,048
-[♪ music ends]
-[cheering and applause]

521
00:29:26,306 --> 00:29:29,934
[♪ serene music playing]

522
00:29:30,018 --> 00:29:33,521
[faint crowd cheering]

523
00:29:34,022 --> 00:29:36,149
<i>I was touring with Blink nonstop.</i>

524
00:29:37,442 --> 00:29:39,277
<i>It was tough...</i>

525
00:29:39,360 --> 00:29:41,780
{\an8}<i>especially since</i>
<i>I was married at the time.</i>

526
00:29:43,740 --> 00:29:48,036
<i>I kinda realized that the relationship</i>
<i>wasn't working for either of us anymore.</i>

527
00:29:49,746 --> 00:29:53,374
I remember we had got into a huge blowout,
