591
00:33:22,125 --> 00:33:24,335
<i>That's how nervous he was then.</i>

592
00:33:25,336 --> 00:33:28,089
Before he ever got on a plane,
he always called me.

593
00:33:28,172 --> 00:33:31,509
<i>I could tell he was</i>
<i>a little on the frightened side.</i>

594
00:33:31,592 --> 00:33:33,553
He probably picked
some of that up from his mother.

595
00:33:36,180 --> 00:33:39,559
[Travis] <i>When I was a kid,</i>
<i>my mom and I flew to Chicago,</i>

596
00:33:39,642 --> 00:33:41,436
and my mom was just in tears.

597
00:33:41,519 --> 00:33:45,314
She was a mess. She hated flying.

598
00:33:46,899 --> 00:33:49,569
<i>I think that, like, zapped me</i>
<i>into hating flying as well</i>

599
00:33:49,652 --> 00:33:51,279
<i>just 'cause I saw my mom hating it</i>

600
00:33:51,362 --> 00:33:53,781
and she was afraid,
and I think at that age you're like,

601
00:33:53,865 --> 00:33:55,324
"I'm afraid, too, then."

602
00:33:56,325 --> 00:33:59,245
♪♪

603
00:34:01,247 --> 00:34:04,375
<i>My friends knew how much</i>
<i>I dreaded being on planes,</i>

604
00:34:04,459 --> 00:34:08,087
