607
00:34:13,009 --> 00:34:14,594
You might even fall asleep."

608
00:34:18,097 --> 00:34:19,724
<i>It started off really mellow</i>
<i>in the beginning.</i>

609
00:34:19,807 --> 00:34:22,226
<i>One or two pills</i>
<i>before we'd go on a flight.</i>

610
00:34:23,686 --> 00:34:25,897
But things didn't stop there at all.

611
00:34:25,980 --> 00:34:28,107
♪♪

612
00:34:32,779 --> 00:34:36,741
<i>It went from taking painkillers</i>
<i>before we'd go on a flight</i>

613
00:34:36,824 --> 00:34:40,661
to actually having to be on 'em
or I couldn't even function.

614
00:34:40,745 --> 00:34:41,913
[inhales deeply]

615
00:34:44,373 --> 00:34:47,835
We were on tour,
and we were takin' a lotta pills.

616
00:34:47,919 --> 00:34:51,172
I couldn't be like,
"Hey, bro, you need to slow down,"

617
00:34:51,255 --> 00:34:55,259
while I'm over here fucking
super fucked up, you know?

618
00:34:58,513 --> 00:34:59,972
[Shanna] <i>He told me, you know,</i>

619
00:35:00,056 --> 00:35:03,059
"I take about 20 to 30 pills
a day sometimes," you know?

620
00:35:03,142 --> 00:35:05,520
And that just was like,
"How are you alive right now?"

621
00:35:07,563 --> 00:35:11,442
[Randalai] <i>I don't know if that was just</i>
<i>part of the whole being famous</i>

622
00:35:11,526 --> 00:35:12,985
<i>and the party scene...</i>

623
00:35:13,569 --> 00:35:16,322
<i>or if it had anything to do</i>
<i>with self-medicating</i>

624
00:35:16,405 --> 00:35:20,409
{\an8}because maybe he was hurting in,
in other ways that we didn't know he was.

625
00:35:20,493 --> 00:35:22,954
{\an8}Whether it was from our mom not being here

626
00:35:23,037 --> 00:35:25,456
or things like that,
I-I honestly don't know.

627
00:35:27,583 --> 00:35:29,836
[Travis] <i>In order for me to sleep,</i>
<i>I would take OxyContin...</i>

628
00:35:30,962 --> 00:35:32,338
<i>to the point where</i>
<i>I felt like I was melting.</i>

629
00:35:35,716 --> 00:35:38,553
<i>I was self-medicating because</i>
<i>I was having to fly almost every day</i>

630
00:35:38,636 --> 00:35:40,388
<i>and be away from my kids.</i>

631
00:35:41,931 --> 00:35:44,100
<i>I was taking so many pills</i>
<i>that I had a security guard</i>

632
00:35:44,183 --> 00:35:46,602
<i>whose only job was to watch me sleep</i>

633
00:35:46,686 --> 00:35:49,272
<i>and make sure I was still breathing.</i>

634
00:35:53,276 --> 00:35:57,697
<i>I started thinking, I might be hitting</i>
<i>a place where I needed to go to rehab.</i>

635
00:36:01,117 --> 00:36:05,496
There was this huge desire
to just quit everything.

636
00:36:07,331 --> 00:36:10,501
<i>But heading back out on tour</i>
<i>and dealing with life on the road</i>

637
00:36:10,585 --> 00:36:12,128
<i>and not being with my kids...</i>

638
00:36:12,962 --> 00:36:14,505
<i>I didn't have the strength.</i>

639
00:36:17,425 --> 00:36:20,178
[♪ vocalizing]

640
00:36:21,137 --> 00:36:25,892
[Mark] <i>In 2005, we were on</i>
<i>this European tour in the dead of winter,</i>

641
00:36:25,975 --> 00:36:27,894
<i>and every single night, we were backstage</i>

642
00:36:27,977 --> 00:36:29,687
{\an8}<i>just screaming at one another.</i>

643
00:36:31,189 --> 00:36:32,940
<i>And we got back from that tour,</i>

644
00:36:33,024 --> 00:36:35,151
and I got a call from our manager saying,

645
00:36:35,234 --> 00:36:37,028
"Tom's not coming.

646
00:36:37,111 --> 00:36:39,322
Tom's done.
He's not, he's not comin' back."

647
00:36:42,825 --> 00:36:46,829
I think at the time, we were
really overworked and just gone a lot.

648
00:36:48,581 --> 00:36:51,000
[Tom] <i>You know, we're exhausted.</i>
<i>We've been working for years.</i>

649
00:36:51,709 --> 00:36:53,294
<i>We weren't all aligned.</i>

650
00:36:53,377 --> 00:36:56,297
<i>I think Travis was</i>
<i>in a different frame of mind at the time</i>

651
00:36:56,380 --> 00:36:57,965
where, you know,
he had his television show,

652
00:36:58,049 --> 00:36:59,717
and he was kind of insatiable.

653
00:37:01,093 --> 00:37:04,639
<i>He wanted to keep going and going</i>
<i>on an everyday basis,</i>

654
00:37:04,722 --> 00:37:06,849
and my family wasn't set up
to support that.

655
00:37:08,184 --> 00:37:09,227
<i>I need to be at home.</i>

656
00:37:09,310 --> 00:37:11,604
I have a daughter, she's two,
and I've been gone this whole time.

657
00:37:11,687 --> 00:37:14,732
And even on our one break,
I did the Box Car Racer record.

658
00:37:15,191 --> 00:37:18,194
{\an8}[♪ "I Feel So" by Box Car Racer playing]

659
00:37:20,988 --> 00:37:24,075
{\an8}[Travis] <i>Tom and I had done</i>
<i>a side project called Box Car Racer.</i>

660
00:37:25,701 --> 00:37:28,120
<i>Box Car was a little heavier</i>
<i>than what Blink was.</i>

661
00:37:28,537 --> 00:37:31,707
<i>♪ Sometimes, I wish I was brave... ♪</i>

662
00:37:31,791 --> 00:37:33,793
<i>And in the back of my head, I wondered,</i>

663
00:37:33,876 --> 00:37:37,004
"How is this gonna go down?
Like, how is this gonna work?"

664
00:37:37,088 --> 00:37:40,383
<i>♪ Wish I was young, wish I was shy... ♪</i>

665
00:37:40,466 --> 00:37:44,679
From my standpoint,
it was everything about Blink except me.

666
00:37:46,180 --> 00:37:49,183
<i>♪ 'Cause I feel so mad... ♪</i>

667
00:37:49,267 --> 00:37:52,478
[Tom] <i>Did the band ever recover</i>
<i>from the Box Car Racer years?</i>

668
00:37:52,561 --> 00:37:55,648
Uh, not the same. No.
You know, I don't think it did.

669
00:37:55,731 --> 00:37:59,402
<i>♪ Let's start over ♪</i>

670
00:38:05,658 --> 00:38:07,493
[Travis] <i>The year Blink broke up,</i>

671
00:38:07,576 --> 00:38:11,330
<i>I had just bought a house</i>
<i>in, like, a nice community</i>

672
00:38:11,414 --> 00:38:12,790
<i>'cause we were having kids, you know?</i>

673
00:38:12,873 --> 00:38:14,667
<i>I think Alabama was just born.</i>

674
00:38:16,168 --> 00:38:18,671
<i>But balancing home life and touring,</i>

675
00:38:18,754 --> 00:38:21,465
<i>our relationship was getting</i>
<i>more and more challenging.</i>

676
00:38:23,092 --> 00:38:24,468
<i>And divorce came soon after.</i>

677
00:38:25,678 --> 00:38:29,140
<i>My marriage fell apart,</i>
<i>my band fell apart.</i>

678
00:38:29,807 --> 00:38:32,768
<i>It felt like my whole world</i>
<i>was falling apart.</i>

679
00:38:33,394 --> 00:38:35,187
[crowd cheering]

680
00:38:35,271 --> 00:38:38,065
{\an8}[♪ "When Your Heart Stops Beating"
by +44 playing]

681
00:38:40,860 --> 00:38:43,529
<i>♪ I'll be there</i>
<i>when your heart stops beating... ♪</i>

682
00:38:43,612 --> 00:38:46,324
<i>I started a project with Mark called +44.</i>

683
00:38:48,367 --> 00:38:50,786
<i>And I had some more time</i>
<i>to focus on a streetwear brand</i>

684
00:38:50,870 --> 00:38:54,332
<i>I started a few years back</i>
<i>called Famous Stars and Straps.</i>

685
00:38:54,415 --> 00:38:56,917
[♪ "Can a Drummer Get Some"
by Travis Barker playing]

686
00:38:58,044 --> 00:39:01,839
[Killer Mike] <i>The Famous F,</i>
<i>the Famous t-shirt, it was everywhere.</i>

687
00:39:02,590 --> 00:39:05,176
{\an8}As a rap fan, you wanted
to show up in a Famous shirt.

688
00:39:06,761 --> 00:39:09,347
8[Nate Diaz] <i>Famous Stars and Straps</i>
<i>was my whole wardrobe.</i>

689
00:39:09,972 --> 00:39:11,807
{\an8}I had probably every shirt they had.

690
00:39:14,060 --> 00:39:16,312
<i>♪ Boom, guess who stepped in the room... ♪</i>

691
00:39:17,438 --> 00:39:19,648
{\an8}[The Game]
<i>There was a kid named Lil' Chris,</i>

692
00:39:19,732 --> 00:39:22,693
{\an8}and what a fucking standup guy
Lil' Chris was, man.

693
00:39:24,403 --> 00:39:26,906
{\an8}[Travis] <i>One day, I'm in the office</i>
<i>in Famous Stars and Straps,</i>

694
00:39:26,989 --> 00:39:29,325
<i>and Nicole, who worked with me</i>
<i>at the time, was like,</i>

695
00:39:29,408 --> 00:39:31,702
<i>"Who's outside washing</i>
<i>your car right now?"</i>

696
00:39:32,703 --> 00:39:36,749
<i>And it's Lil' Chris. He had, like,</i>
<i>figured out where my office was.</i>

697
00:39:36,832 --> 00:39:38,250
<i>So I went out</i>,<i> and I said,</i>
<i>"Hey, what's up, man?"</i>

698
00:39:38,334 --> 00:39:39,752
<i>He's like, "Hey, what's up?"</i>

699
00:39:39,835 --> 00:39:41,754
<i>He'd say, "Yo, I wash cars.</i>

700
00:39:41,837 --> 00:39:44,173
<i>I'm gonna come by all the time</i>
<i>and make sure your cars are cleaned."</i>

701
00:39:44,256 --> 00:39:46,008
And I'm like, "Oh, I don't need
my car cleaned, though.

702
00:39:46,092 --> 00:39:47,843
Everything's okay.
Like, you don't need to clean my car."

703
00:39:47,927 --> 00:39:49,678
He's like, "No, I'm gonna
prove myself to you."

704
00:39:49,762 --> 00:39:52,556
And I said, "Well, you're not
washing my car for free."

705
00:39:53,557 --> 00:39:56,268
<i>And then I'm like,</i>
<i>"This motherfucker is just like me."</i>

706
00:39:56,352 --> 00:39:58,562
He doesn't... [chuckles]
He's, like-- doesn't stop.

707
00:39:58,646 --> 00:40:02,483
<i>He's so determined,</i>
<i>and he's so motivated every day.</i>

708
00:40:02,775 --> 00:40:06,028
<i>I was like, "This is my second half,</i>
<i>like my right hand."</i>

709
00:40:06,570 --> 00:40:09,198
<i>He was into, like, lowriders</i>
<i>and skateboarding.</i>

710
00:40:09,740 --> 00:40:10,825
<i>Everything I was into.</i>

711
00:40:11,951 --> 00:40:14,161
[Tim] <i>They were, like, inseparable.</i>

712
00:40:14,245 --> 00:40:16,664
They were like a buddy movie come to life.

713
00:40:16,747 --> 00:40:18,624
[slight chuckle] For real, man.

714
00:40:19,166 --> 00:40:22,586
Me and Trav, we're out the door.
We've got meetings, meetings, meetings.

715
00:40:22,670 --> 00:40:24,588
[Travis] <i>So, I hired him as my assistant,</i>

716
00:40:24,672 --> 00:40:28,509
<i>and we never spent, like, a day away</i>
<i>from each other from that point on.</i>

717
00:40:29,802 --> 00:40:31,554
<i>He was like a brother to me.</i>

718
00:40:31,637 --> 00:40:33,055
<i>♪ Can a drummer get some? ♪</i>

719
00:40:34,265 --> 00:40:35,975
[The Game] <i>He had Lil' Chris</i>
<i>running from studio to studio</i>

720
00:40:36,058 --> 00:40:39,395
<i>with these big bags of clothes</i>
<i>for all the hip-hop artists.</i>

721
00:40:40,521 --> 00:40:44,066
And I think that that was, um, his intro
in the hip-hop world, to be honest.

722
00:40:45,359 --> 00:40:48,112
[tattoo machine buzzing]

723
00:40:48,821 --> 00:40:53,701
[Mister Cartoon] <i>He would show up at,</i>
<i>like, all rap crew, Psycho Realm.</i>

724
00:40:53,784 --> 00:40:55,619
{\an8}We would see him through
all those different spots.

725
00:40:55,703 --> 00:40:58,247
{\an8}So, like, he knew
about those hardcore gigs.

726
00:40:59,707 --> 00:41:02,001
<i>Like, puts it together</i>
<i>with the black Cadillac,</i>

727
00:41:02,084 --> 00:41:04,003
<i>rollin' in, inked up.</i>

728
00:41:04,795 --> 00:41:07,173
<i>He was a tattoo maniac.</i>

729
00:41:07,256 --> 00:41:09,467
<i>He was one</i>
<i>of the first celebrities I've known</i>

730
00:41:09,550 --> 00:41:11,093
to blast the side of their head.

731
00:41:12,428 --> 00:41:14,972
<i>Travis showed that he was</i>
<i>way ahead of the curve</i>

732
00:41:15,055 --> 00:41:17,057
<i>by doing it way back then.</i>

733
00:41:18,142 --> 00:41:23,564
<i>That's what made him stand out:</i>
<i>classic cars, tattoo culture,</i>

734
00:41:24,148 --> 00:41:27,193
<i>music, everything together.</i>

735
00:41:27,276 --> 00:41:30,696
<i>♪♪</i>

736
00:41:30,779 --> 00:41:33,741
[Travis] <i>I had been told for so long</i>
<i>that there's a drum machine</i>

737
00:41:33,824 --> 00:41:36,202
<i>that takes the place</i>
<i>for drums in rap music.</i>

738
00:41:37,286 --> 00:41:39,205
<i>I had pretty much counted myself out.</i>

739
00:41:40,206 --> 00:41:42,416
<i>It was kinda around that time,</i>
<i>Rob hit me and he said,</i>

740
00:41:42,500 --> 00:41:47,129
<i>"Yo, Bun and Pimp want you</i>
<i>to make a beat for Bun's album."</i>

741
00:41:47,922 --> 00:41:49,507
I was like, "I don't really make beats."

742
00:41:49,590 --> 00:41:51,800
And he's like,
"Well, now you do." [laughs]

743
00:41:51,884 --> 00:41:54,178
-[audience cheering]
-[♪ "Forever" playing]

744
00:41:54,261 --> 00:41:55,304
{\an8}[Drake] I got 'em.

745
00:41:55,387 --> 00:41:58,641
{\an8}<i>♪ Last name Ever, first name Greatest ♪</i>

746
00:41:58,724 --> 00:42:01,143
{\an8}<i>♪ Like a sprained ankle, boy,</i>
<i>I ain't nothin' to play with ♪</i>

747
00:42:01,227 --> 00:42:02,394
<i>♪ I started... ♪</i>

748
00:42:02,478 --> 00:42:03,854
[Travis]
<i>If Bun and Pimp didn't challenge me,</i>

749
00:42:03,938 --> 00:42:07,233
<i>I probably would have never even</i>
<i>attempted to make a rap beat.</i>

750
00:42:07,733 --> 00:42:10,361
<i>-♪ I'm in your city, faded off the brown ♪</i>
<i>-♪ Nino ♪</i>

751
00:42:10,444 --> 00:42:14,114
But once I did, it just kept
going crazy from there.

752
00:42:16,283 --> 00:42:19,370
At that point, I think I was playing
with every rapper I was listening to.

753
00:42:20,454 --> 00:42:24,166
<i>I was finally able to contribute</i>
<i>to another genre of music I grew up on.</i>

754
00:42:24,250 --> 00:42:26,335
[♪ rapping]

755
00:42:26,418 --> 00:42:28,671
-[airhorn blaring]
-[Eminem] Let's go.

756
00:42:28,754 --> 00:42:29,964
<i>♪ There they go ♪</i>

757
00:42:30,047 --> 00:42:31,882
<i>♪ Packin' stadiums</i>
<i>as Shady spits his flow... ♪</i>

758
00:42:31,966 --> 00:42:33,717
[Killer Mike] <i>That drum matters in rap.</i>

759
00:42:33,801 --> 00:42:36,095
<i>The fact that he understands</i>
<i>the subtle nuances</i>

760
00:42:36,178 --> 00:42:38,973
<i>between what rock tracks demand on drums</i>

761
00:42:39,056 --> 00:42:41,642
<i>and what programming drums demand on drums</i>

762
00:42:41,725 --> 00:42:45,229
says a lot about his duality
and dexterity.

763
00:42:45,312 --> 00:42:47,022
Because usually,
rock drummers don't get it.

764
00:42:47,106 --> 00:42:50,234
<i>♪ Back into the game, and they know rap</i>
<i>will never be the same as befo' ♪</i>

765
00:42:50,317 --> 00:42:53,112
<i>♪ Bashin' in the brains of these...</i>
<i>and establishin' a name as he goes... ♪</i>

766
00:42:53,654 --> 00:42:56,198
[Travis] <i>My strengths lie</i>
<i>in listening to everything</i>

767
00:42:56,282 --> 00:42:57,700
<i>and taking from everything.</i>

768
00:42:57,783 --> 00:42:59,368
<i>♪ ...that I'm talkin' about when we riot ♪</i>

769
00:42:59,451 --> 00:43:02,204
<i>♪ I'm Hannibal Lecter, so just in case</i>
<i>you're thinkin' of savin' face ♪</i>

770
00:43:02,288 --> 00:43:03,581
<i>♪ You ain't gonna have no face to save ♪</i>

771
00:43:03,664 --> 00:43:05,416
<i>♪ By the time I'm through</i>
<i>with this place, so, Drake ♪</i>

772
00:43:06,709 --> 00:43:09,128
<i>♪ I want this shit forever, mane ♪</i>

773
00:43:10,879 --> 00:43:13,215
[Travis] <i>My goal would be</i>
<i>to be the most recorded</i>

774
00:43:13,299 --> 00:43:14,800
<i>and collaborative drummer.</i>

775
00:43:16,135 --> 00:43:17,678
[♪ record scratching]

776
00:43:17,761 --> 00:43:20,681
{\an8}-[♪ "Stay Fly" by Three 6 Mafia playing]
<i>-♪ I gotta stay fly-y-y-y-y-y-y-y-y-y... ♪</i>

777
00:43:20,764 --> 00:43:24,351
{\an8}Now I had met Adam a few times, DJ AM.

778
00:43:24,435 --> 00:43:28,397
<i>♪ I gotta stay fly-y-y-y-y-y-y-y-y-y... ♪</i>

779
00:43:28,480 --> 00:43:31,650
<i>At the time, AM was, like,</i>
<i>the hottest DJ in LA.</i>

780
00:43:31,734 --> 00:43:34,445
<i>♪ Fly-y-y-y-y-y-y-y-y-y ♪</i>

781
00:43:34,528 --> 00:43:36,363
<i>♪ 'Til I die-ie-ie-ie-ie-ie-ie... ♪</i>

782
00:43:36,447 --> 00:43:38,157
He would hit every genre of music.

783
00:43:39,867 --> 00:43:43,621
Watching AM play, like, records
that no one would dare play

784
00:43:43,704 --> 00:43:47,291
and making them sound cooler
than they ever sounded,

785
00:43:47,374 --> 00:43:49,084
already had my wheels spinning.

786
00:43:49,168 --> 00:43:51,378
♪♪

787
00:43:52,671 --> 00:43:55,674
<i>He could fill up a room, read the room,</i>

788
00:43:55,758 --> 00:43:56,967
and make them go crazy.

789
00:43:57,051 --> 00:43:59,511
♪♪

790
00:44:02,598 --> 00:44:03,599
<i>♪ Here we go ♪</i>

791
00:44:05,684 --> 00:44:06,894
<i>Sure enough, we linked.</i>

792
00:44:07,853 --> 00:44:10,189
<i>And I said, "Yo, I got this crazy idea.</i>

793
00:44:10,272 --> 00:44:14,568
<i>"Drummer-DJ duo where</i>
<i>you're just throwin' records at me,</i>

794
00:44:14,652 --> 00:44:16,236
<i>"and I provide the beat,</i>

795
00:44:16,320 --> 00:44:18,697
<i>"and we just kind of remix records live,</i>

796
00:44:18,781 --> 00:44:21,450
<i>but leave no genre untouched."</i>

797
00:44:21,533 --> 00:44:24,578
[audience cheering]

798
00:44:25,204 --> 00:44:26,955
<i>We got into a rehearsal space.</i>

799
00:44:27,790 --> 00:44:30,834
We didn't stop playing
for, like, four to five hours.

800
00:44:30,918 --> 00:44:34,338
♪♪

801
00:44:50,979 --> 00:44:52,439
<i>I don't think we spoke.</i>

802
00:44:53,273 --> 00:44:55,484
<i>He was speaking through his turntables,</i>

803
00:44:56,110 --> 00:44:57,528
and I was speaking through my drums.

804
00:44:59,238 --> 00:45:02,449
[♪ "Ring of Fire" playing]

805
00:45:02,533 --> 00:45:03,992
[Tommy Lee] <i>I remember seeing them</i>

806
00:45:04,076 --> 00:45:08,539
<i>and having the drums playing</i>
<i>on top and in between,</i>

807
00:45:08,622 --> 00:45:13,085
<i>it just added this,</i>
<i>like, whole other element.</i>

808
00:45:13,794 --> 00:45:16,422
{\an8}It was fuckin' rad. [laughs]

809
00:45:19,925 --> 00:45:23,595
[Travis] <i>Adam was the greatest.</i>
<i>He was one of the nicest dudes ever.</i>

810
00:45:23,679 --> 00:45:25,264
Super positive.

811
00:45:26,140 --> 00:45:29,476
<i>♪ Love is a burning thing ♪</i>

812
00:45:30,853 --> 00:45:32,104
<i>♪ And it makes... ♪</i>

813
00:45:32,187 --> 00:45:34,648
[Kevin Wolff]
<i>Their personalities, so similar.</i>

814
00:45:34,732 --> 00:45:37,484
<i>They'd laugh at the same jokes,</i>
<i>same type of sense of humor.</i>

815
00:45:39,319 --> 00:45:41,905
[Travis] <i>We were very much cut</i>
<i>from the same cloth, you know,</i>

816
00:45:41,989 --> 00:45:45,117
except he was sober and I wasn't.

817
00:45:45,200 --> 00:45:48,287
♪♪

818
00:45:51,415 --> 00:45:52,416
[♪ music stops]

819
00:45:57,504 --> 00:46:00,591
[Kevin] <i>Throughout his sobriety,</i>
<i>which was over 10 years,</i>

820
00:46:00,674 --> 00:46:04,887
<i>he did always talk about</i>
<i>how he was still struggling.</i>

821
00:46:06,638 --> 00:46:10,184
{\an8}I think any addict will, will tell you
that, you know, it's,

822
00:46:10,267 --> 00:46:13,979
{\an8}it's, it's one day at a time,
and that demon is always there.

823
00:46:16,398 --> 00:46:18,817
[Travis] <i>This is the one dude</i>
<i>who challenged me to be sober.</i>

824
00:46:19,651 --> 00:46:21,945
<i>He would actually make me be sober</i>

825
00:46:22,029 --> 00:46:26,074
for 48-hour periods of time
before I made big decisions.

826
00:46:27,993 --> 00:46:30,704
[Lawrence]
<i>AM really took his sobriety seriously.</i>

827
00:46:31,371 --> 00:46:35,334
{\an8}AM really wanted Travis to just
not have that be a part of his life.

828
00:46:35,417 --> 00:46:37,503
<i>Not because it would affect</i>
<i>AM's life so much.</i>

829
00:46:38,545 --> 00:46:41,131
<i>He knew how much better a father,</i>

830
00:46:41,215 --> 00:46:43,592
<i>how much better a businessman,</i>
<i>how much better a musician</i>

831
00:46:43,675 --> 00:46:46,595
<i>Travis would be</i>
<i>if he got that out of his life.</i>

832
00:46:48,806 --> 00:46:50,933
[Travis]<i> I remember sitting</i>
<i>with my clothing attorney</i>

833
00:46:51,016 --> 00:46:53,477
<i>and my music attorney.</i>

834
00:46:53,560 --> 00:46:56,939
They basically came and said, like,
"We're worried about you.

835
00:46:58,273 --> 00:47:00,150
<i>"Things are a little excessive right now,</i>

836
00:47:00,234 --> 00:47:01,902
<i>"like the drug use, the pills.</i>

837
00:47:01,985 --> 00:47:04,112
<i>We just wanna make sure</i>
<i>everything's okay."</i>

838
00:47:04,196 --> 00:47:06,281
And I remember being like,
"What the fuck are you guys talking about?

839
00:47:06,365 --> 00:47:10,953
Like, everything's fine.
Like, I'm a functioning addict I guess."

840
00:47:12,579 --> 00:47:15,415
<i>But deep down, I wondered</i>
<i>what it'd be like if I didn't do anything.</i>

841
00:47:15,499 --> 00:47:17,960
<i>How good I'd be at running,</i>
<i>how good I'd be at boxing,</i>

842
00:47:18,043 --> 00:47:19,378
how good I'd be at drumming.

843
00:47:19,461 --> 00:47:24,258
But... in my mind, I'd also accepted
I don't think I'll ever know.

844
00:47:24,341 --> 00:47:27,177
[♪ somber music playing]

845
00:47:31,682 --> 00:47:35,894
[Lawrence] <i>The boys had gotten booked</i>
<i>to do a private event.</i>

846
00:47:36,520 --> 00:47:41,483
AM was on the road for a while,
and he was meeting Travis there.

847
00:47:43,151 --> 00:47:45,821
[Travis]<i> I was like,</i>
<i>"I don't even know if I wanna go."</i>

848
00:47:45,904 --> 00:47:47,781
"Like, all these gigs
that I have to fly to?

849
00:47:47,865 --> 00:47:50,868
I just, I feel like
I just want them to go away."

850
00:47:51,535 --> 00:47:53,871
<i>I just want to be at home with my kids.</i>

851
00:47:54,872 --> 00:47:58,041
<i>Before I left, my daughter,</i>
<i>Alabama, was hysterically crying</i>

852
00:47:58,125 --> 00:47:59,251
<i>and just saying, like,</i>

853
00:47:59,334 --> 00:48:01,461
"The roof is on fire,
and it's gonna come off."

854
00:48:01,545 --> 00:48:04,965
And it was just the weirdest thing,
and she was hysterically crying.

855
00:48:06,675 --> 00:48:09,511
<i>She cried for, like,</i>
<i>two hours straight after I had left.</i>

856
00:48:11,930 --> 00:48:13,599
[Kevin] <i>Travis actually flew in private.</i>

857
00:48:14,057 --> 00:48:15,809
<i>He flew in with Lil' Chris and Che.</i>

858
00:48:17,311 --> 00:48:20,898
{\an8}[Travis] <i>Che was one</i>
<i>of my really good friends</i>

859
00:48:20,981 --> 00:48:24,318
{\an8}<i>that started touring with me as security.</i>

860
00:48:26,528 --> 00:48:29,531
{\an8}<i>The show was awesome.</i>
<i>It was outdoors.</i>

861
00:48:29,615 --> 00:48:31,116
<i>It was a really good time.</i>

862
00:48:31,950 --> 00:48:35,245
But I think it was maybe 9:00 or 10:00,

863
00:48:35,329 --> 00:48:36,663
and the whole event was over.

864
00:48:38,749 --> 00:48:41,710
You know, I'd seen Lil' Chris
and AM gathering together,

865
00:48:41,793 --> 00:48:44,296
and they were both like,
"Dude, let's try to go home tonight."

866
00:48:45,964 --> 00:48:47,174
<i>And I said, "Whatever you guys wanna do,</i>

867
00:48:47,257 --> 00:48:51,011
<i>I'll-I'll roll with the punches,</i>
<i>but I'm cool to just chill."</i>

868
00:48:52,554 --> 00:48:54,348
Basically did a majority rules.

869
00:48:54,431 --> 00:48:58,018
Who wants to fly home?
Who doesn't? I lost. [chuckles]

870
00:48:58,101 --> 00:49:02,105
Um, but I was a team player.
I said, "I'll-I'll roll, whatever."

871
00:49:04,650 --> 00:49:07,861
<i>We leave the hotel,</i>
<i>we go over to the airport,</i>

872
00:49:07,945 --> 00:49:10,739
and it's, like, dark.

873
00:49:10,822 --> 00:49:13,659
It's almost midnight, I think.
We're supposed to leave at midnight.

874
00:49:15,202 --> 00:49:17,829
<i>There's all these big, nice planes,</i>

875
00:49:17,913 --> 00:49:19,539
<i>and then it's, like, foggy and weird,</i>

876
00:49:19,623 --> 00:49:21,333
<i>and there's this little plane</i>
[slight chuckle]

877
00:49:21,416 --> 00:49:23,001
in the corner, and I was like,

878
00:49:23,085 --> 00:49:25,921
"Man, I pray to God that's not
our fucking plane over there."

879
00:49:26,004 --> 00:49:28,632
And then, sure enough,
the dude drives past

880
00:49:28,715 --> 00:49:32,719
all the big, nice planes and, of course,
drives to that fucking plane.

881
00:49:32,803 --> 00:49:35,305
[♪ tense music playing]

882
00:49:36,431 --> 00:49:38,976
{\an8}<i>We smoke out, we hotboxed</i>
<i>the driver's car.</i>

883
00:49:40,852 --> 00:49:42,187
<i>We get out.</i>

884
00:49:42,854 --> 00:49:44,439
Chris takes a picture in front of it.

885
00:49:46,358 --> 00:49:49,069
<i>And he's like, "Fuck, this plane's sketch.</i>

886
00:49:49,152 --> 00:49:51,822
Like, we're on the smallest plane
at this fucking airport."

887
00:49:52,322 --> 00:49:53,824
I call my dad.

888
00:49:54,241 --> 00:49:55,867
He said, "Dad," he says, uh...

889
00:49:56,827 --> 00:49:58,453
And sent me a picture of the plane.

890
00:49:59,705 --> 00:50:01,623
He says, "This is,
this is what we're gettin' on."

891
00:50:01,707 --> 00:50:04,209
He says, "I-I don't really
wanna get on this plane."

892
00:50:07,379 --> 00:50:08,714
I told him if something happens,

893
00:50:08,797 --> 00:50:11,550
like, make sure everything's cool
with the kids, you know?

894
00:50:13,010 --> 00:50:14,011
And, uh...

895
00:50:16,930 --> 00:50:20,934
that was definitely, uh, emotional
for whatever reason.

896
00:50:21,018 --> 00:50:23,270
When I called him, and he was like,
"Hey, wha-what's going on with you?"

897
00:50:23,353 --> 00:50:24,938
And I said, "I don't know, Pal.
I just have, like..."

898
00:50:25,022 --> 00:50:26,356
[sniffles]

899
00:50:34,573 --> 00:50:36,825
[voice breaking] I just said,
"I have a weird feeling," you know?

900
00:50:39,745 --> 00:50:42,372
[drum roll]

901
00:50:54,217 --> 00:50:55,552
<i>We got on the plane.</i>

902
00:50:56,845 --> 00:51:01,767
It was Chris, Che, Adam, and myself.

903
00:51:01,850 --> 00:51:03,643
And I always sit by emergency exits

904
00:51:03,727 --> 00:51:05,979
'cause I'm... [inhales deeply]
I'm a fucking weirdo.

905
00:51:10,525 --> 00:51:13,445
<i>I've always done that since I ever,</i>
<i>you know, had to get on a plane.</i>

906
00:51:16,865 --> 00:51:18,366
<i>I had smoked and drank.</i>

907
00:51:19,117 --> 00:51:21,328
I think took, like,
a Xanax bar and a Vicodin.

908
00:51:22,329 --> 00:51:24,748
So I'm awake.
I think I'm almost dozing off

909
00:51:24,831 --> 00:51:26,500
when we finally take off.

910
00:51:26,583 --> 00:51:29,002
♪♪

911
00:51:30,003 --> 00:51:33,423
[jet engines whirring]

912
00:51:36,635 --> 00:51:38,637
<i>The thing I probably</i>
<i>hate most about flying</i>

913
00:51:38,720 --> 00:51:40,722
is just the rumbling of the jets

914
00:51:40,806 --> 00:51:43,767
and you just know you're about
to haul ass down a runway

915
00:51:43,850 --> 00:51:45,769
and fly up into the air.

916
00:51:45,852 --> 00:51:47,854
♪♪

917
00:51:47,938 --> 00:51:50,190
[engines roaring]

918
00:51:54,236 --> 00:51:56,738
I hear really loud, like, gunshot noises.

919
00:52:02,577 --> 00:52:04,788
I feel it getting very rough.

920
00:52:04,871 --> 00:52:07,916
I guess, at this point,
the landing gear had blown up.

921
00:52:09,793 --> 00:52:13,463
The belly of the plane
is basically on the ground skidding,

922
00:52:13,547 --> 00:52:15,674
and it, it catches fire.

923
00:52:17,217 --> 00:52:20,220
And the plane attempted
to take off to go in the air,

924
00:52:20,303 --> 00:52:23,515
and then we'd go down,
go in the air, go down.

925
00:52:23,598 --> 00:52:25,433
[airplane whooshing]

926
00:52:26,601 --> 00:52:29,020
And we end up hitting an embankment.

927
00:52:29,104 --> 00:52:31,231
♪♪

928
00:52:35,443 --> 00:52:37,529
Just fire and chaos everywhere.

929
00:52:40,740 --> 00:52:43,827
I couldn't go in front of me,
so I went to the side of me.

930
00:52:45,787 --> 00:52:47,289
<i>AM was knocked out.</i>

931
00:52:47,372 --> 00:52:49,833
He had hit his head, so I-I grabbed him

932
00:52:49,916 --> 00:52:51,960
and I shook him, and he woke up.

933
00:52:54,379 --> 00:52:56,131
<i>Tried to make my way in front of him.</i>

934
00:52:57,132 --> 00:52:59,843
The lower parts of my arms caught fire.

935
00:53:03,471 --> 00:53:05,473
I went to the emergency exit,
and I opened it.

936
00:53:07,934 --> 00:53:11,229
<i>Jumped out right into the jet</i>
<i>where all the fuel is.</i>

937
00:53:12,105 --> 00:53:13,440
Then, my whole body caught fire.

938
00:53:14,232 --> 00:53:16,735
[flames whooshing]

939
00:53:18,028 --> 00:53:20,864
I'm running,
and the fire just won't go out.

940
00:53:25,619 --> 00:53:28,413
<i>I stopped, dropped, and rolled,</i>
<i>and then AM came out,</i>

941
00:53:28,496 --> 00:53:30,415
and he patted my feet off fire.

942
00:53:34,294 --> 00:53:37,047
Maybe 10 seconds later,
the plane blows up.

943
00:53:37,130 --> 00:53:39,174
[cymbals crashing]

944
00:53:49,935 --> 00:53:52,479
-[fire truck horn blaring]
-[sirens wailing]

945
00:54:12,666 --> 00:54:14,251
[Randy] <i>My heart sunk.</i>

946
00:54:14,501 --> 00:54:17,420
I-- You know, I thought I have lost a son.

947
00:54:19,673 --> 00:54:22,008
{\an8}[announcer]
<i>Live from ABC 7.</i>

948
00:54:22,092 --> 00:54:25,011
{\an8}[reporter 1] <i>Four people are dead</i>
<i>and two critically injured.</i>

949
00:54:25,345 --> 00:54:28,223
{\an8}[reporter 2] <i>Barker and DJ AM,</i>
<i>whose real name is Adam Goldstein,</i>

950
00:54:28,306 --> 00:54:31,226
{\an8}<i>are in critical condition at a burn center</i>
<i>in Augusta, Georgia.</i>

951
00:54:32,727 --> 00:54:35,397
{\an8}[Tom] <i>I was in North Carolina</i>
<i>boarding a plane,</i>

952
00:54:35,480 --> 00:54:39,901
{\an8}and on the television
outside the gate, it just pops up,

953
00:54:39,985 --> 00:54:42,112
and it's, like, playing and it's the text,

954
00:54:42,195 --> 00:54:46,366
and it's CNN and all this shit,
and I was just frozen.

955
00:54:47,492 --> 00:54:50,620
♪♪

956
00:54:56,209 --> 00:54:58,795
[Dr. Peter Grossman]
<i>Travis was in really bad shape.</i>

957
00:54:59,879 --> 00:55:02,382
{\an8}These weren't just little burns
that he had.

958
00:55:02,465 --> 00:55:05,427
{\an8}These were extensive burns to his legs,

959
00:55:05,510 --> 00:55:07,804
{\an8}his feet, his buttocks,
his arms, his hands.

960
00:55:08,471 --> 00:55:12,100
<i>And there was an absolute concern</i>

961
00:55:12,183 --> 00:55:15,228
<i>as to whether or not,</i>
<i>uh, he would survive.</i>

962
00:55:17,397 --> 00:55:20,233
[♪ dark music playing]

963
00:55:24,237 --> 00:55:26,072
[Travis]
<i>My brain really wasn't functioning.</i>

964
00:55:28,158 --> 00:55:30,702
I was on morphine,
and I was on all sorts of medicine,

965
00:55:30,785 --> 00:55:34,497
so I didn't even really understand...

966
00:55:34,581 --> 00:55:36,082
the severity of it all.

967
00:55:38,626 --> 00:55:40,837
<i>I'd broke all of my ribs.</i>

968
00:55:42,255 --> 00:55:44,674
<i>Fractured my back</i>
<i>in four different places.</i>

969
00:55:46,885 --> 00:55:48,762
They couldn't do any more surgeries,

970
00:55:48,845 --> 00:55:49,971
and I was low on blood...

971
00:55:52,724 --> 00:55:54,934
<i>and then there was talks</i>
<i>of amputating my foot.</i>

972
00:55:56,895 --> 00:55:59,022
Sixty-five percent of my body was burnt.

973
00:56:04,110 --> 00:56:07,155
♪♪

974
00:56:11,576 --> 00:56:14,996
It was fucked up, you know? He, uh...

975
00:56:18,249 --> 00:56:23,755
As soon as I walked in and seen him,
I start crying, you know, and, um...

976
00:56:23,838 --> 00:56:26,007
[inhales deeply]

977
00:56:28,802 --> 00:56:31,221
[Dr. Brian Weeks] <i>Burn injuries</i>
<i>are probably the worst type of injury</i>

978
00:56:31,304 --> 00:56:32,639
<i>that anybody could suffer.</i>

979
00:56:33,640 --> 00:56:35,433
{\an8}You know, we've all burned
our finger with a blister

980
00:56:35,517 --> 00:56:36,684
{\an8}and, and knows what happens to that.

981
00:56:36,768 --> 00:56:39,020
{\an8}Well, imagine that with 65% of your body.

982
00:56:41,356 --> 00:56:43,400
[Dr. Grossman] <i>Clinically,</i>
<i>they were all third-degree burns,</i>

983
00:56:43,858 --> 00:56:45,985
<i>which means we had to remove that skin.</i>

984
00:56:47,445 --> 00:56:50,115
In order to do that, you basically
have to shave away that skin.

985
00:56:50,198 --> 00:56:52,325
You take these knives and you shave away.

986
00:56:52,409 --> 00:56:53,743
You're skinning the patient.

987
00:56:56,079 --> 00:56:57,789
<i>When you take those skin grafts,</i>

988
00:56:57,872 --> 00:57:01,459
you're exposing nerve endings,
and that's very painful.

989
00:57:01,543 --> 00:57:03,503
So now, he's got pain in his burn areas

990
00:57:03,586 --> 00:57:06,214
<i>and pain from the areas</i>
<i>where we harvested his skin.</i>

991
00:57:08,550 --> 00:57:10,301
[Travis] <i>I was in a lot of pain.</i>

992
00:57:11,344 --> 00:57:12,679
<i>They couldn't get</i>
<i>my pain management right,</i>

993
00:57:12,762 --> 00:57:14,139
<i>so I was freaking out.</i>

994
00:57:16,182 --> 00:57:19,644
The normal amount
of pain medicine was not affecting him

995
00:57:20,311 --> 00:57:24,774
and then, giving him even more
wasn't relieving his pain.

996
00:57:25,817 --> 00:57:29,737
<i>It became apparent to me</i>
<i>that this was someone whose body</i>

997
00:57:29,821 --> 00:57:33,199
<i>was now physiologically addicted</i>
<i>to pain medication.</i>

998
00:57:35,076 --> 00:57:37,203
[Travis] <i>I was basically,</i>
<i>like, on the same drugs</i>

999
00:57:37,287 --> 00:57:39,581
<i>I was on every day,</i>
<i>so I could feel everything.</i>

1000
00:57:40,957 --> 00:57:42,459
<i>It was all a blur.</i>

1001
00:57:43,168 --> 00:57:46,588
What had happened or who was alive,
I had no clue.

1002
00:57:49,466 --> 00:57:51,926
<i>And then, obviously,</i>
<i>"Well, where's Chris and Che?"</i>

1003
00:57:54,304 --> 00:57:55,930
And, um...

1004
00:58:01,186 --> 00:58:04,564
[Tim] <i>His sister invited me down</i>
<i>to go to the burn unit,</i>

1005
00:58:05,607 --> 00:58:07,609
<i>and I walk in the room.</i>

1006
00:58:09,027 --> 00:58:11,029
Then I go, "Man, Lil' Chris."

1007
00:58:12,489 --> 00:58:13,990
[exhales sharply]

1008
00:58:16,493 --> 00:58:19,662
<i>And I don't cry ever, and he don't cry.</i>

1009
00:58:21,247 --> 00:58:22,707
But we cried, bro.

1010
00:58:25,251 --> 00:58:27,462
<i>That was about as sad as it gets.</i>

1011
00:58:31,132 --> 00:58:33,343
[Travis] <i>Che and Lil' Chris</i>
<i>were like brothers to me.</i>

1012
00:58:34,511 --> 00:58:37,222
<i>I was closer to Chris</i>
<i>than anyone in my entire life.</i>

1013
00:58:39,140 --> 00:58:40,975
[Linda Warn] <i>They were inseparable.</i>

1014
00:58:42,310 --> 00:58:45,146
<i>They had so much fun always.</i>

1015
00:58:47,106 --> 00:58:52,737
{\an8}Travis took Chris's dreams
and expectations and made them real.

1016
00:58:54,864 --> 00:58:56,199
{\an8}[sniffles]

1017
00:58:58,034 --> 00:59:00,328
[Lawrence] <i>Lil' Chris and Che's passing</i>
<i>was hard on everyone,</i>

1018
00:59:00,411 --> 00:59:02,372
<i>but it killed Travis.</i>

1019
00:59:02,455 --> 00:59:03,748
<i>Just killed him that he couldn't...</i>

1020
00:59:04,249 --> 00:59:08,253
You know, Chris is having a funeral in LA,
and Travis is still at the burn center.

1021
00:59:08,920 --> 00:59:11,548
♪♪

1022
00:59:14,217 --> 00:59:16,761
Even though he was physically recovering

1023
00:59:16,844 --> 00:59:18,429
and was getting in
a better place, physically,

1024
00:59:18,513 --> 00:59:20,306
every time I went to see him,
he seemed to be doing

1025
00:59:20,390 --> 00:59:23,309
a little worse, uh, emotionally.

1026
00:59:24,727 --> 00:59:27,647
He would, you know,
try to put on a brave face,

1027
00:59:27,730 --> 00:59:31,651
but he didn't know if he would
ever play the drums again.

1028
00:59:31,734 --> 00:59:33,570
He didn't know if he'd,
you know, be able to do

1029
00:59:33,653 --> 00:59:35,822
all these things he dreamed
of doing with his kids.

1030
00:59:37,615 --> 00:59:40,368
[Travis] <i>I couldn't see my kids</i>
<i>'cause 65% of my body</i>

1031
00:59:40,451 --> 00:59:41,911
<i>was an open wound.</i>

1032
00:59:42,745 --> 00:59:44,956
<i>I was handling that miserably.</i>

1033
00:59:48,209 --> 00:59:50,837
I was suicidal
when I was in the hospital...

1034
00:59:53,131 --> 00:59:56,050
<i>and I was there for another</i>
<i>three and a half months,</i>

1035
00:59:56,676 --> 00:59:59,804
<i>and I had 27 surgeries there.</i>

1036
01:00:01,848 --> 01:00:05,893
There was a few times where he was
just ready to call it a day, you know?

1037
01:00:05,977 --> 01:00:09,564
"Bring me a gun," and blah-blah.
But I was like, "Fuck, no."

1038
01:00:11,274 --> 01:00:15,695
"I'll transfer any amount of money,
just fuckin' kill me."

1039
01:00:22,327 --> 01:00:24,162
[Dr. Briere] <i>You know,</i>
<i>it's really hard to put a pin</i>

1040
01:00:24,245 --> 01:00:26,539
<i>on how long it's gonna take</i>
<i>anyone to recover.</i>

1041
01:00:28,291 --> 01:00:31,794
<i>The danger, though, is if when we try</i>
<i>to say you're better or you're not,</i>

1042
01:00:31,878 --> 01:00:32,879
<i>you're recovered when you're not</i>

1043
01:00:32,962 --> 01:00:35,715
<i>because, frankly, even if you think</i>
<i>about your own childhood</i>

1044
01:00:35,798 --> 01:00:37,967
{\an8}when something happened to you then,
is it completely gone now?

1045
01:00:38,051 --> 01:00:39,469
{\an8}It probably isn't in its own way.

1046
01:00:41,346 --> 01:00:43,806
<i>So, we're all kinda makin'</i>
<i>our own deal with the devil here</i>

1047
01:00:43,890 --> 01:00:46,225
<i>in terms of what we can tolerate,</i>
<i>what we can handle,</i>

1048
01:00:46,309 --> 01:00:48,061
<i>and how we can move on from it.</i>

1049
01:00:51,773 --> 01:00:54,192
[Lawrence] <i>AM would confide in me a lot,</i>

1050
01:00:54,275 --> 01:00:55,985
<i>and AM was really worried.</i>

1051
01:00:56,069 --> 01:00:59,113
You know, "I don't know if Travis
is gonna be Travis again."

1052
01:00:59,739 --> 01:01:02,825
[♪ poignant music playing]

1053
01:01:04,077 --> 01:01:07,997
[Dr. Grossman]
<i>Adam was different than Travis.</i>

1054
01:01:08,956 --> 01:01:11,626
<i>His burns were not as extensive</i>

1055
01:01:11,709 --> 01:01:13,920
<i>and was in the hospital</i>
<i>for a shorter period of time.</i>

1056
01:01:14,629 --> 01:01:19,634
<i>Interestingly, Adam was calm</i>
<i>and almost subdued.</i>

1057
01:01:20,635 --> 01:01:22,011
<i>There was two extremes.</i>

1058
01:01:22,095 --> 01:01:25,306
One who was very im--
traumatized by the accident,

1059
01:01:25,390 --> 01:01:29,352
and one who was almost, um, uh,
disassociating himself from it.

1060
01:01:31,521 --> 01:01:34,315
[Travis] <i>He was in the burn center</i>
<i>for a week and a half,</i>

1061
01:01:35,066 --> 01:01:36,150
<i>and he was out.</i>

1062
01:01:36,234 --> 01:01:37,402
<i>It was really quick.</i>

1063
01:01:38,319 --> 01:01:41,948
<i>And I think he flew a week later.</i>

1064
01:01:43,908 --> 01:01:47,245
And that was a shock to me.
I just couldn't believe it, you know?

1065
01:01:47,328 --> 01:01:51,332
I just couldn't comprehend
how he was getting on a plane.

1066
01:01:54,460 --> 01:01:57,463
[Lawrence] <i>You know, Jay-Z had asked AM</i>
<i>to go on tour with him,</i>

1067
01:01:57,547 --> 01:01:59,632
and he was supposed to go, like,
three weeks after the crash.

1068
01:02:01,426 --> 01:02:03,720
<i>I'm trying to convince AM,</i>
<i>"We could tour on buses.</i>

1069
01:02:03,803 --> 01:02:05,555
<i>You don't need to do this anymore."</i>

1070
01:02:07,390 --> 01:02:09,892
<i>The part that drove him</i>
<i>wasn't the financial side.</i>

1071
01:02:09,976 --> 01:02:11,853
<i>It was the-the star.</i>

1072
01:02:11,936 --> 01:02:15,481
<i>It was, "I want to perform</i>
<i>for everybody all around the world."</i>

1073
01:02:18,067 --> 01:02:22,071
<i>Performing for people is what allowed him</i>
<i>to be sober in a weird way.</i>

1074
01:02:23,281 --> 01:02:24,949
At the time, that was, that was AM's drug.

1075
01:02:28,244 --> 01:02:30,455
[Travis] <i>We met up</i>
<i>right when I got out of the hospital.</i>

1076
01:02:31,122 --> 01:02:34,250
<i>We shared stories</i>
<i>and just kinda talked about it.</i>

1077
01:02:35,668 --> 01:02:38,755
<i>He had told me he was seeing</i>
<i>a new therapist.</i>

1078
01:02:39,213 --> 01:02:40,923
<i>And this new therapist had told him, like,</i>

1079
01:02:41,007 --> 01:02:42,967
<i>"Look, man, you've been in a plane crash.</i>

1080
01:02:43,050 --> 01:02:47,472
I don't think it's so bad if you,
if you take a Xanax before you fly."

1081
01:02:50,558 --> 01:02:52,810
<i>You know, we gave each other</i>
<i>a hug and he was like...</i>

1082
01:02:52,894 --> 01:02:54,896
<i>You know, I said,</i>
<i>"I'll see, I'll see you in New York."</i>

1083
01:02:56,689 --> 01:02:57,815
And he's like, "Yeah."

1084
01:02:57,899 --> 01:02:59,192
He's like, "But, you know,

1085
01:02:59,275 --> 01:03:01,903
"honestly, I just feel like doin'
a shit ton of drugs

1086
01:03:01,986 --> 01:03:03,362
and saying fuck it."

1087
01:03:05,907 --> 01:03:09,535
<i>There was no kinda</i>
<i>funny punchline at the end.</i>

1088
01:03:13,372 --> 01:03:14,791
[Lawrence] <i>Something was off.</i>

1089
01:03:15,666 --> 01:03:17,877
<i>Kevy, who was AM's best friend,</i>

1090
01:03:18,544 --> 01:03:20,171
you know, he calls me and he says,

1091
01:03:20,254 --> 01:03:22,256
"Dude, [sighs] I think he's using."

1092
01:03:24,550 --> 01:03:26,969
<i>You know, the next day,</i>
<i>we find his sponsor.</i>

1093
01:03:28,554 --> 01:03:30,890
<i>Kevy, myself, and his sponsor</i>
<i>fly out to New York...</i>

1094
01:03:31,641 --> 01:03:34,936
<i>go right to his apartment,</i>
<i>and he's not answering BBM.</i>

1095
01:03:35,603 --> 01:03:37,021
<i>He's not answering his phone.</i>

1096
01:03:38,397 --> 01:03:41,234
<i>We can't get to his door</i>
<i>'cause the doorman won't let us up.</i>

1097
01:03:43,069 --> 01:03:45,029
You know, finally it was like,
"You know what? Fuck this.

1098
01:03:45,112 --> 01:03:46,322
Call the police."

1099
01:03:47,156 --> 01:03:50,993
Police go upstairs...
bang down the door...

1100
01:03:52,662 --> 01:03:55,873
<i>and... it's too late.</i>

1101
01:03:58,084 --> 01:04:00,086
[♪ somber music playing]

1102
01:04:00,169 --> 01:04:03,381
[Travis] <i>I was in New York</i>
<i>working on an album,</i>

1103
01:04:03,464 --> 01:04:06,551
and Daniel, my drum tech,
came and handed me the computer.

1104
01:04:06,634 --> 01:04:09,512
I don't know if it was
TMZ or something, but

1105
01:04:09,595 --> 01:04:12,598
they basically said, um...

1106
01:04:18,437 --> 01:04:21,107
[Lawrence]
<i>You know, I remember that night...</i>

1107
01:04:21,190 --> 01:04:22,984
<i>Travis couldn't even speak.</i>

1108
01:04:23,818 --> 01:04:25,361
I could hardly speak.

1109
01:04:26,487 --> 01:04:29,282
[♪ somber music continues]

1110
01:04:29,365 --> 01:04:36,080
[Travis] <i>After AM passed, it was</i>
<i>beyond difficult to relate to anybody.</i>

1111
01:04:37,456 --> 01:04:40,960
<i>I really had no one.</i>
<i>I would exhaust post-traumatic doctors.</i>

1112
01:04:41,043 --> 01:04:46,173
And I would... just hit walls constantly.

1113
01:04:49,385 --> 01:04:53,222
<i>I just, honestly, wanted</i>
<i>to lock myself in the hotel room.</i>

1114
01:04:53,806 --> 01:04:56,392
<i>I had lost another one</i>
<i>of my closest friends.</i>

1115
01:04:56,475 --> 01:04:59,979
<i>I felt like I was in </i>Final Destination,
<i>and I was gonna be next.</i>

1116
01:05:00,062 --> 01:05:01,564
<i>♪♪</i>

1117
01:05:09,447 --> 01:05:12,158
[Lawrence] <i>It got way worse</i>
<i>after AM passed away</i>

1118
01:05:12,241 --> 01:05:15,369
<i>'cause Travis had</i>
<i>this weird sense of, like,</i>

1119
01:05:15,953 --> 01:05:19,165
<i>"I was supposed to die. Why am I here?</i>

1120
01:05:19,707 --> 01:05:21,334
Why am I the only survivor?"

1121
01:05:23,169 --> 01:05:25,880
[Travis] <i>I definitely had feelings</i>
<i>of survivor's guilt.</i>

1122
01:05:25,963 --> 01:05:27,506
<i>I was beating myself up.</i>

1123
01:05:27,840 --> 01:05:29,216
<i>Like, that was my main thing.</i>

1124
01:05:29,300 --> 01:05:31,385
<i>"Well, why am I here</i>
<i>and everyone else isn't?"</i>

1125
01:05:32,345 --> 01:05:35,932
I had to believe that I am
still here for a reason.

1126
01:05:38,184 --> 01:05:41,520
[♪ mournful music playing]

1127
01:05:50,363 --> 01:05:53,240
<i>Before he passed away,</i>

1128
01:05:53,324 --> 01:05:55,660
<i>our best therapy</i>
<i>was talking amongst each other.</i>

1129
01:05:58,162 --> 01:06:01,332
<i>We would talk about everything</i>
<i>from how hard it was</i>

1130
01:06:01,415 --> 01:06:03,417
<i>for me to walk down a street</i>

1131
01:06:03,501 --> 01:06:06,212
<i>without thinking planes</i>
<i>were gonna fall out of the sky</i>

1132
01:06:07,088 --> 01:06:09,840
<i>to, "Should I tour again?"</i>

1133
01:06:09,924 --> 01:06:11,801
<i>Do you wanna leave the house?</i>

1134
01:06:13,094 --> 01:06:14,303
<i>When is enough enough?</i>

1135
01:06:15,805 --> 01:06:17,264
<i>You've already done so much.</i>

1136
01:06:18,349 --> 01:06:20,059
<i>What else is there left to do?</i>

1137
01:06:20,601 --> 01:06:23,062
<i>Those were all the things</i>
<i>I kinda had to ask myself,</i>

1138
01:06:23,145 --> 01:06:25,731
<i>like, who I was gonna be</i>
<i>after this accident.</i>

1139
01:06:29,151 --> 01:06:32,780
<i>AM had said, "For me,</i>
<i>I feel like I don't have much to live for,</i>

1140
01:06:32,863 --> 01:06:36,492
<i>"and it's really,</i>
<i>you know, fuckin' with me.</i>

1141
01:06:37,702 --> 01:06:40,871
<i>You know, you got kids,</i>
<i>you have a lot to live for."</i>

1142
01:06:41,914 --> 01:06:44,750
[♪ mournful music continues]

1143
01:06:50,798 --> 01:06:52,466
<i>I just didn't leave the kids.</i>

1144
01:06:53,968 --> 01:06:55,845
<i>I would sleep in Landon's bed...</i>

1145
01:06:57,471 --> 01:06:59,098
<i>and then I would sleep in Alabama's bed.</i>

1146
01:06:59,181 --> 01:07:00,433
<i>I would just go back and forth.</i>

1147
01:07:02,893 --> 01:07:05,146
<i>I wouldn't spend a minute away from 'em.</i>

1148
01:07:08,524 --> 01:07:12,153
<i>I'd hired a driver to take them to school</i>
<i>'cause I couldn't drive,</i>

1149
01:07:12,236 --> 01:07:13,988
<i>and I would just lay</i>
<i>in the back of the car,</i>

1150
01:07:14,071 --> 01:07:16,240
and I just was with them
everywhere they went.

1151
01:07:20,661 --> 01:07:22,872
<i>My kids really kept me together.</i>

1152
01:07:24,290 --> 01:07:26,042
<i>It was honestly</i>

1153
01:07:26,125 --> 01:07:27,960
<i>the best thing for my recovery and</i>

1154
01:07:28,919 --> 01:07:30,921
<i>the best thing to give me strength.</i>

1155
01:07:33,549 --> 01:07:36,510
<i>I never wanted to feel as high</i>
<i>as I did in the hospital again.</i>

1156
01:07:37,344 --> 01:07:39,764
<i>I didn't want anything</i>
<i>to do with painkillers.</i>

1157
01:07:40,431 --> 01:07:42,058
<i>I flushed those down the toilet.</i>

1158
01:07:43,184 --> 01:07:45,019
<i>I was not gonna fail my kids.</i>

1159
01:07:46,312 --> 01:07:47,938
<i>I really had to bounce back.</i>

1160
01:07:49,231 --> 01:07:52,068
[waves crashing]

1161
01:07:52,610 --> 01:07:56,113
[laughter]

1162
01:07:56,781 --> 01:07:58,824
[kisses smack]

1163
01:07:59,533 --> 01:08:00,993
-Ew.
-[Travis] Mm.

1164
01:08:01,077 --> 01:08:03,037
-[Alabama Barker] His armpits stink.
-[laughs]

1165
01:08:03,120 --> 01:08:04,872
-[Travis] Yeah, get some of that.
-Ew, that's gross.

1166
01:08:04,955 --> 01:08:05,998
[laughs]

1167
01:08:06,082 --> 01:08:07,583
And why do they smell so bad?

1168
01:08:08,417 --> 01:08:09,835
Didn't you shower last night?

1169
01:08:09,919 --> 01:08:11,378
[laughs]

1170
01:08:11,462 --> 01:08:13,881
-What are you doing?
-I played drums all night.

1171
01:08:14,256 --> 01:08:15,466
You didn't shower last night?

1172
01:08:15,549 --> 01:08:16,801
Yeah, I did.

1173
01:08:17,802 --> 01:08:20,179
Why do you smell? You smell really bad.

1174
01:08:20,262 --> 01:08:21,931
[laughs]

1175
01:08:22,014 --> 01:08:23,557
[Tom] <i>With each passing day,</i>

1176
01:08:23,641 --> 01:08:25,810
<i>he started coming back to who he was.</i>

1177
01:08:26,435 --> 01:08:28,479
Right, left, right, right, left.

1178
01:08:28,562 --> 01:08:31,482
Right, right, right,
left, right, right. No.

1179
01:08:31,565 --> 01:08:33,901
Right, right, right, right,
right, right, left.

1180
01:08:33,984 --> 01:08:36,612
No. You have to practice it
over and over again.

1181
01:08:37,613 --> 01:08:41,117
After the accident,
the things he craved were different,

1182
01:08:41,200 --> 01:08:43,577
and they were more
along the lines of somebody

1183
01:08:43,661 --> 01:08:44,954
that got their priorities straight.

1184
01:08:45,037 --> 01:08:47,039
[drumsticks tapping rhythmically]

1185
01:08:50,501 --> 01:08:52,128
[Travis]
Told you. It's in your blood, son.

1186
01:08:55,923 --> 01:08:59,218
[Atiana De La Hoya] <i>You could definitely</i>
<i>tell that something was different.</i>

1187
01:09:00,427 --> 01:09:02,346
<i>I don't know how I could pinpoint it,</i>

1188
01:09:02,429 --> 01:09:04,765
{\an8}but it changed for the whole family,

1189
01:09:04,849 --> 01:09:08,602
{\an8}and I feel like kind of brought us
closer together in a sense.

1190
01:09:09,353 --> 01:09:12,481
[♪ upbeat music playing]

1191
01:09:19,280 --> 01:09:22,783
{\an8}We loved him trying to cook for us...

1192
01:09:24,034 --> 01:09:25,661
<i>going on bike rides.</i>

1193
01:09:27,246 --> 01:09:30,124
[Atiana] <i>He would always take us</i>
<i>to school in his low ride cars.</i>

1194
01:09:31,208 --> 01:09:34,003
Whenever my friends would come over,
they'd always be so scared of him,

1195
01:09:34,086 --> 01:09:35,754
<i>and then, now that they've gotten</i>
<i>to know him, they're like,</i>

1196
01:09:35,838 --> 01:09:38,257
<i>"I don't know why</i>
<i>I was ever scared of Travis."</i>

1197
01:09:40,259 --> 01:09:43,053
{\an8}I went on my first tour,
I think I was, like, four years old.

1198
01:09:44,430 --> 01:09:47,433
<i>It's really cool to see him</i>
<i>going to Europe.</i>

1199
01:09:48,350 --> 01:09:50,019
<i>We always take the boat.</i>

1200
01:09:51,687 --> 01:09:53,439
[Travis] <i>They've done every tour with me.</i>

1201
01:09:53,522 --> 01:09:55,399
<i>They've done punk rock tours,</i>

1202
01:09:55,482 --> 01:09:59,111
<i>they've done hip-hop tours,</i>
<i>all sorts of stuff, man.</i>

1203
01:09:59,653 --> 01:10:01,280
<i>They've kinda came everywhere with me.</i>

1204
01:10:03,616 --> 01:10:06,202
[Atiana] <i>He used to smoke a lot</i>
<i>and drink and party and stuff.</i>

1205
01:10:07,161 --> 01:10:09,205
Now, he's, like, completely the opposite.

1206
01:10:09,288 --> 01:10:11,874
I mean, he doesn't drink, smoke.

1207
01:10:11,957 --> 01:10:13,500
He's completely vegan.

1208
01:10:15,794 --> 01:10:18,130
[Travis]
<i>Being sober at this part of my life,</i>

1209
01:10:18,214 --> 01:10:20,341
<i>for my children, is so important.</i>

1210
01:10:21,759 --> 01:10:24,178
<i>You know, everyone is looking</i>
<i>at you, right?</i>

1211
01:10:25,262 --> 01:10:26,889
<i>And especially for my kids...</i>

1212
01:10:28,307 --> 01:10:31,810
the best is not to tell them,
but, but to show 'em.

1213
01:10:35,940 --> 01:10:38,359
<i>After my accident,</i>
<i>I figured out a lot of things.</i>

1214
01:10:39,235 --> 01:10:40,945
<i>How do I become a better human?</i>

1215
01:10:41,445 --> 01:10:43,113
How do I become a healthier human?

1216
01:10:47,034 --> 01:10:48,786
<i>There was, like, checkmarks.</i>

1217
01:10:48,869 --> 01:10:50,496
<i>It was like, "You're not</i>
<i>gonna play drums again.</i>

1218
01:10:50,579 --> 01:10:53,290
<i>You won't run again.</i>
<i>You might not be able to do this again."</i>

1219
01:10:55,459 --> 01:10:57,670
<i>Just crossing them off one by one,</i>

1220
01:10:58,295 --> 01:11:00,506
that's the journey that I've been on.

1221
01:11:02,841 --> 01:11:04,593
[Toby Morse]
<i>I've known Travis through everything.</i>

1222
01:11:05,886 --> 01:11:07,388
<i>We always talk about running together.</i>

1223
01:11:08,472 --> 01:11:11,433
<i>I invited him to this thing</i>
<i>called, uh, 2 Bears 5K.</i>

1224
01:11:12,268 --> 01:11:14,895
{\an8}The race took off, and I was like,
I'm just gonna run, like, a sexy pace,

1225
01:11:14,979 --> 01:11:16,272
{\an8}like, you know, a dad pace.

1226
01:11:17,606 --> 01:11:20,484
<i>He just, like, smoked everybody.</i>

1227
01:11:21,485 --> 01:11:24,113
In that moment, I was like,
"Holy shit, dude. This dude's a runner."

1228
01:11:24,196 --> 01:11:27,116
And since then, he's doing
all these Run Travis Runs.

1229
01:11:29,034 --> 01:11:32,371
<i>The same kinda misfits and punk rockers</i>
<i>that would come to see Blink-182</i>

1230
01:11:32,454 --> 01:11:35,874
<i>are now coming to run</i>
<i>with Travis Barker and get healthy.</i>

1231
01:11:38,294 --> 01:11:41,338
[Travis] <i>Running marathons</i>
<i>is a way of processing trauma.</i>

1232
01:11:41,797 --> 01:11:43,215
<i>It gives me control again.</i>

1233
01:11:43,799 --> 01:11:47,052
<i>Instead of that pain being imposed on me,</i>
<i>I'm running towards it.</i>

1234
01:11:48,512 --> 01:11:49,888
<i>It's therapeutic to me.</i>

1235
01:11:51,098 --> 01:11:53,267
[tattoo machine buzzing]

1236
01:11:55,477 --> 01:11:56,687
[Mister Cartoon]
What are we doin' today?

1237
01:11:56,770 --> 01:11:58,230
I don't know. I'm covered.

1238
01:11:58,314 --> 01:12:00,941
-[laughter]
-I'm just, like, tattooing over shit,

1239
01:12:01,025 --> 01:12:03,068
but I still have, like...
I still have my legs.

1240
01:12:03,152 --> 01:12:05,070
-Like, I did both kneecaps.
-Yeah.

1241
01:12:06,155 --> 01:12:08,365
Another tough area you have here.

1242
01:12:09,283 --> 01:12:10,492
[Travis] It's not bad.

1243
01:12:11,785 --> 01:12:15,080
When I grew up, you know,
tattoos were gang-related

1244
01:12:15,164 --> 01:12:18,250
or, you know, guys that were in prison.

1245
01:12:19,501 --> 01:12:23,714
<i>But all these tattoos that's on him</i>
<i>has to do with his life in music.</i>

1246
01:12:24,798 --> 01:12:27,843
[♪ gentle music playing]

1247
01:12:27,926 --> 01:12:30,095
<i>He came out one year for Christmas.</i>

1248
01:12:30,179 --> 01:12:32,389
He said, "Dad," he said,
"Got somethin' to show you."

1249
01:12:34,183 --> 01:12:37,311
<i>When he was just a little boy, we always</i>
<i>referred to one another as "Pal."</i>

1250
01:12:38,645 --> 01:12:41,690
So, he took his shirt off
and he said, "Look,"

1251
01:12:41,774 --> 01:12:44,193
and he had "Pal" tattooed right here.

1252
01:12:46,862 --> 01:12:49,448
[chuckling] Well, at least
he got one good tattoo anyhow.

1253
01:12:51,158 --> 01:12:53,494
[Travis] <i>After the accident,</i>
<i>my dad and I kept getting</i>

1254
01:12:53,577 --> 01:12:55,412
<i>closer and closer and closer.</i>

1255
01:12:56,121 --> 01:12:58,123
<i>He's definitely my rock.</i>

1256
01:12:59,124 --> 01:13:00,542
[Randy] <i>He calls me every day.</i>

1257
01:13:01,043 --> 01:13:02,878
Every single day.

1258
01:13:02,961 --> 01:13:05,547
He calls me before he goes
on stage to play,

1259
01:13:05,631 --> 01:13:06,965
and he tells me he loves me.

1260
01:13:07,049 --> 01:13:09,259
I tell him I love him, you know.

1261
01:13:11,053 --> 01:13:15,057
One day, I went,
"Come here, I got somethin' to show you."

1262
01:13:17,643 --> 01:13:19,812
<i>And he said, "Dad, that's a sticker."</i>

1263
01:13:19,895 --> 01:13:21,647
<i>I said, "No, that's not a sticker."</i>

1264
01:13:22,731 --> 01:13:24,233
I decided, you know,

1265
01:13:24,316 --> 01:13:26,276
just to show him
I support him and everything,

1266
01:13:26,360 --> 01:13:28,404
that I'm gonna go
and I'm gonna get that done.

1267
01:13:29,530 --> 01:13:31,698
I feel just about as proud as I could be.

1268
01:13:34,451 --> 01:13:38,455
[Travis] <i>Well, lookin' back on it now,</i>
<i>my dad was tough on me,</i>

1269
01:13:38,539 --> 01:13:42,793
<i>but what seemed hard at the time</i>
<i>really made me the man I am today.</i>

1270
01:13:45,087 --> 01:13:46,713
[Randy] <i>Travis is my son,</i>

1271
01:13:47,548 --> 01:13:50,384
and, uh, you know,
I love my son very much.

1272
01:13:50,884 --> 01:13:53,137
-[group] Aw.
-And I told him,

1273
01:13:53,220 --> 01:13:57,224
"When you find somebody
like your mother, you hang on to it."

1274
01:13:58,058 --> 01:14:00,436
And so, now he's got that,
and he's hanging onto it.

1275
01:14:00,519 --> 01:14:02,271
[group] Aww.

1276
01:14:02,354 --> 01:14:04,440
[cheering and applause]

1277
01:14:05,315 --> 01:14:08,652
[♪ playing upbeat tune]

1278
01:14:11,071 --> 01:14:13,991
[Kourtney Kardashian Barker]
<i>When I first met Travis,</i>

1279
01:14:14,074 --> 01:14:17,161
he was just very gentle and quiet,

1280
01:14:17,911 --> 01:14:21,415
{\an8}which doesn't match up with his exterior

1281
01:14:21,498 --> 01:14:22,833
{\an8}of what you would think he would be.

1282
01:14:22,916 --> 01:14:24,751
[♪ gentle piano music playing]

1283
01:14:25,878 --> 01:14:28,172
[Travis] <i>We lived down the street</i>
<i>from each other.</i>

1284
01:14:28,255 --> 01:14:29,381
<i>I was friends with her,</i>

1285
01:14:29,465 --> 01:14:32,259
and I've known her
and her family for a long time.

1286
01:14:33,552 --> 01:14:36,096
<i>I would spend a lot of holidays with her.</i>

1287
01:14:36,180 --> 01:14:37,306
[speaker] Look at Travis go.

1288
01:14:37,681 --> 01:14:40,392
Halloween and Christmas, we thrived.

1289
01:14:40,476 --> 01:14:42,519
[chuckling] Like, those were our seasons.

1290
01:14:43,437 --> 01:14:45,230
We'd carve pumpkins with the kids,

1291
01:14:45,856 --> 01:14:48,901
<i>and we would decorate gingerbread houses.</i>

1292
01:14:49,443 --> 01:14:51,737
It was a string. It's a strand of light.

1293
01:14:53,572 --> 01:14:58,702
<i>Watching him as a father,</i>
<i>that always drew me to him.</i>

1294
01:14:59,620 --> 01:15:03,624
<i>I got to know his real values</i>
<i>through his kids.</i>

1295
01:15:04,875 --> 01:15:06,710
[Travis] <i>All my guy friends would be like,</i>

1296
01:15:06,793 --> 01:15:08,795
<i>"Man, what are you guys waitin' for?"</i>

1297
01:15:09,421 --> 01:15:12,382
I would literally come home
from the studio at 6:00 a.m.

1298
01:15:12,466 --> 01:15:14,801
from working all night
and wake up two hours later

1299
01:15:14,885 --> 01:15:16,970
to work out with her
just 'cause I wanted to see her.

1300
01:15:19,014 --> 01:15:22,643
{\an8}<i>I always thought to myself,</i>
<i>if this ever happens,</i>

1301
01:15:22,726 --> 01:15:26,813
<i>it was gonna be bigger</i>
<i>than we could ever imagine.</i>

1302
01:15:28,315 --> 01:15:31,985
<i>Just by the interaction as friends,</i>

1303
01:15:32,069 --> 01:15:34,863
<i>just by lookin' in her eyes,</i>
<i>I knew she was the one.</i>

1304
01:15:36,114 --> 01:15:38,200
[♪ gentle music playing]

1305
01:15:46,333 --> 01:15:48,085
<i>We fell madly in love.</i>

1306
01:15:49,127 --> 01:15:52,339
<i>I felt like I had superpowers,</i>

1307
01:15:52,422 --> 01:15:54,383
<i>like I was a kid all over again.</i>

1308
01:15:55,551 --> 01:15:57,469
[Kourtney shrieks]

1309
01:15:58,929 --> 01:16:01,974
[Kourtney] <i>Six months into being together,</i>

1310
01:16:02,057 --> 01:16:04,851
we found out that we were pregnant.

1311
01:16:05,143 --> 01:16:06,603
We're having a baby.

1312
01:16:06,687 --> 01:16:09,064
-What?!
-[all cheering]

1313
01:16:14,945 --> 01:16:18,865
[Kourtney]
<i>And everything just made so much sense.</i>

1314
01:16:19,783 --> 01:16:21,410
<i>We were so happy.</i>

1315
01:16:23,161 --> 01:16:25,372
[Travis] <i>We were</i>
<i>about three months pregnant,</i>

1316
01:16:25,455 --> 01:16:27,874
<i>and she was gonna be a little girl,</i>

1317
01:16:27,958 --> 01:16:30,711
<i>and we had decided to name her Tulip.</i>

1318
01:16:30,794 --> 01:16:32,254
And we go to the doctor,

1319
01:16:32,337 --> 01:16:34,923
and the doctor tells us

1320
01:16:35,007 --> 01:16:36,508
the baby doesn't have a heartbeat.

1321
01:16:39,803 --> 01:16:42,639
[♪ solemn music playing]

1322
01:16:44,391 --> 01:16:48,812
[Kourtney] <i>When we lost the baby,</i>
<i>we were devastated.</i>

1323
01:16:49,813 --> 01:16:53,150
We just laid in bed and cried for days.

1324
01:16:56,236 --> 01:16:59,865
<i>All we wanted was to have a baby together.</i>

1325
01:17:03,160 --> 01:17:08,040
<i>I was 41, and I remember my doctor saying,</i>
<i>"You have to do IVF."</i>

1326
01:17:09,124 --> 01:17:10,751
Confirm name and date of birth.

1327
01:17:10,834 --> 01:17:12,169
-Yeah. That's my date of birth.
-Okay.

1328
01:17:12,252 --> 01:17:13,712
Just put the sample in this cup

1329
01:17:13,795 --> 01:17:15,172
and then, when you're done,
just place it on that counter

1330
01:17:15,255 --> 01:17:16,423
and I'll come and grab it for you.

1331
01:17:16,506 --> 01:17:19,217
[Kourtney] <i>It was so hard on my body.</i>

1332
01:17:19,301 --> 01:17:22,471
<i>We tried five times over eight months</i>

1333
01:17:22,554 --> 01:17:25,140
<i>and it felt like my body</i>
<i>was shutting down.</i>

1334
01:17:25,223 --> 01:17:29,269
[doctor] This one is small.
Very unlikely to get a mature egg.

1335
01:17:30,270 --> 01:17:32,773
[Travis] <i>They're like,</i>
<i>"You have less eggs every month."</i>

1336
01:17:32,856 --> 01:17:36,485
And it was like, "Oh, gosh."
Like, this is so discouraging.

1337
01:17:37,235 --> 01:17:40,238
Let's cover this
so we can do your ultrasound.

1338
01:17:41,114 --> 01:17:46,328
[Kourtney] <i>Each time we would try it,</i>
<i>it just felt so disappointing.</i>

1339
01:17:47,454 --> 01:17:50,874
<i>It really did something</i>
<i>that messed with me mentally.</i>

1340
01:17:52,834 --> 01:17:56,838
<i>And I remember crying to Travis,</i>
<i>"I can't do this anymore."</i>

1341
01:17:58,715 --> 01:18:03,303
I just said to him,
"If God has a baby in store for us,

1342
01:18:03,387 --> 01:18:05,972
<i>it will happen, naturally."</i>

1343
01:18:08,600 --> 01:18:11,937
[waves crashing]

1344
01:18:13,188 --> 01:18:16,566
[Travis] <i>A year after being together,</i>
<i>I asked Kourtney to marry me</i>

1345
01:18:17,693 --> 01:18:20,028
<i>and we shifted all of our energy</i>
<i>into the wedding.</i>

1346
01:18:21,530 --> 01:18:24,825
[♪ upbeat, romantic music playing]

1347
01:18:40,006 --> 01:18:43,385
<i>After my accident, there was</i>
<i>a lot of "no way, no hows."</i>

1348
01:18:44,302 --> 01:18:46,179
<i>I never thought</i>
<i>I was gonna get married again.</i>

1349
01:18:46,263 --> 01:18:48,223
<i>I never planned on having</i>
<i>any more children.</i>

1350
01:18:49,808 --> 01:18:52,811
<i>And then, I fell in love</i>
<i>with my best friend.</i>

1351
01:18:56,398 --> 01:18:59,109
<i>It just started opening my eyes</i>
<i>and my world.</i>

1352
01:19:00,485 --> 01:19:03,321
Sounds corny,
but it's just like a fairytale story.

1353
01:19:03,405 --> 01:19:05,323
♪♪

1354
01:19:11,830 --> 01:19:14,583
{\an8}[crowd cheering]

1355
01:19:14,666 --> 01:19:17,294
[♪ rock music playing]

1356
01:19:21,506 --> 01:19:22,924
[Mark] Hey. Hey, Travis.

1357
01:19:23,008 --> 01:19:24,259
[band member]
We've got an announcement here!

1358
01:19:24,342 --> 01:19:25,677
[Tom] Hey, Travis!

1359
01:19:25,761 --> 01:19:28,388
[Mark] Hey, Travis.

1360
01:19:30,140 --> 01:19:33,810
[Kourtney] <i>A year after stopping IVF,</i>

1361
01:19:33,894 --> 01:19:37,689
<i>we got pregnant, naturally,</i>
<i>on Valentine's Day.</i>

1362
01:19:38,190 --> 01:19:39,816
[Mark] Whoa. Hey, calm down.

1363
01:19:39,900 --> 01:19:43,069
[whistling]

1364
01:19:43,153 --> 01:19:45,071
[Travis]
<i>For me, it was kinda unbelievable.</i>

1365
01:19:46,782 --> 01:19:47,991
<i>It was a miracle.</i>

1366
01:19:48,575 --> 01:19:52,454
[drumroll]

1367
01:19:53,538 --> 01:19:56,541
[crowd cheering]

1368
01:19:57,918 --> 01:20:00,170
[Travis]
<i>Once you've experienced a miscarriage,</i>

1369
01:20:00,253 --> 01:20:01,588
you're just waiting, you know?

1370
01:20:01,671 --> 01:20:05,133
You're waiting
for something awful to happen.

1371
01:20:05,217 --> 01:20:07,552
[warbling]

1372
01:20:08,470 --> 01:20:10,806
[Kourtney]
<i>I think because all of his trauma</i>

1373
01:20:10,889 --> 01:20:12,891
<i>and everything he's been through,</i>

1374
01:20:12,974 --> 01:20:15,977
he was really worried the whole pregnancy.

1375
01:20:18,021 --> 01:20:19,356
[Travis] Is that his little hand?

1376
01:20:19,439 --> 01:20:21,066
[doctor] [over phone]
<i>Yeah, it's in a fist.</i>

1377
01:20:21,149 --> 01:20:22,901
[Kourtney] [over phone]
<i>We're waiting for it to open up</i>

1378
01:20:22,984 --> 01:20:24,736
{\an8}<i>so he can look at all the bones.</i>

1379
01:20:25,529 --> 01:20:28,865
{\an8}[Travis] <i>We got into seven months,</i>
<i>and I was touring.</i>

1380
01:20:28,949 --> 01:20:32,244
I was actually in Europe, and she says,

1381
01:20:32,327 --> 01:20:36,122
"Trav, I-I went to my doctor

1382
01:20:36,206 --> 01:20:40,627
and the baby's lungs
are filling with fluid."

1383
01:20:40,710 --> 01:20:42,879
[♪ tense music playing]

1384
01:20:42,963 --> 01:20:47,175
It was terrifying
going in for the surgery.

1385
01:20:48,301 --> 01:20:51,555
[Travis] <i>They did this surgery</i>
<i>where they drained</i>

1386
01:20:51,638 --> 01:20:53,223
<i>the fluid from his lungs</i>

1387
01:20:53,306 --> 01:20:56,142
<i>by placing a needle through her stomach.</i>

1388
01:20:57,352 --> 01:20:59,980
<i>The whole time, I was preparing myself.</i>

1389
01:21:02,274 --> 01:21:04,901
[Kourtney] <i>They canceled four shows,</i>

1390
01:21:04,985 --> 01:21:07,696
and he just came
and laid with me in the hospital

1391
01:21:07,779 --> 01:21:11,950
and was there with me
and made sure that everything was okay.

1392
01:21:14,744 --> 01:21:15,829
Mm.

1393
01:21:15,912 --> 01:21:17,914
Rocky's gonna come out doin' front kicks.

1394
01:21:20,876 --> 01:21:23,336
<i>The surgery was a success, thank God.</i>

1395
01:21:25,005 --> 01:21:26,631
<i>And Rocky was born one month later.</i>

1396
01:21:28,884 --> 01:21:31,595
[Kourtney] <i>They had told us,</i>
<i>you're probably gonna be in the hospital</i>

1397
01:21:31,678 --> 01:21:35,307
<i>for eight weeks, at the minimum.</i>

1398
01:21:36,057 --> 01:21:38,935
[Travis] <i>We were in the NICU for a week</i>

1399
01:21:39,019 --> 01:21:41,396
<i>and then we went home</i>
<i>and we've never been back.</i>

1400
01:21:41,479 --> 01:21:45,191
He's like the healthiest, happiest
little human I've ever met.

1401
01:21:46,401 --> 01:21:49,905
[♪ upbeat music playing]

1402
01:21:49,988 --> 01:21:52,616
<i>And the whole time Rocky was in her belly,</i>

1403
01:21:52,699 --> 01:21:54,034
he was listenin' to me practice.

1404
01:21:54,117 --> 01:21:55,118
I would play for him.

1405
01:21:59,623 --> 01:22:02,500
<i>God blessed us with this healthy,</i>
<i>beautiful baby boy.</i>

1406
01:22:03,460 --> 01:22:06,212
[Kourtney]
<i>Having Rocky gives him another chance</i>

1407
01:22:06,296 --> 01:22:09,758
<i>to do what he loves most and does best:</i>

1408
01:22:09,841 --> 01:22:11,051
<i>being a father.</i>

1409
01:22:12,761 --> 01:22:15,221
Go. Yes.

1410
01:22:15,305 --> 01:22:17,599
[Kourtney] <i>Being able to experience life</i>

1411
01:22:17,682 --> 01:22:21,269
<i>through a baby's eyes all over again,</i>

1412
01:22:22,145 --> 01:22:24,773
<i>every experience feels new.</i>

1413
01:22:26,274 --> 01:22:27,901
<i>It changes you.</i>

1414
01:22:30,570 --> 01:22:34,741
<i>There's never a dull moment</i>
<i>in this big, blended family.</i>

1415
01:22:34,824 --> 01:22:37,410
[Travis] [laughs]
My pants are falling down.

1416
01:22:38,411 --> 01:22:42,040
<i>She has three children.</i>
<i>I have three children.</i>

1417
01:22:42,123 --> 01:22:44,501
<i>And then, we have Rocky.</i>

1418
01:22:45,251 --> 01:22:47,462
<i>We all live together in one house.</i>

1419
01:22:48,797 --> 01:22:50,715
<i>It's basically </i>The Brady Bunch.

1420
01:22:52,300 --> 01:22:54,594
[Atiana]
<i>Do you remember </i>The Brady Bunch?

1421
01:22:54,678 --> 01:22:56,388
<i>The family that had, like, the van,</i>

1422
01:22:56,471 --> 01:22:58,139
<i>and, like, they'd</i>
<i>all show up together and, like--</i>

1423
01:22:58,223 --> 01:23:00,141
-We're so much cooler than that family.
-[Atiana] We're-- It's--

1424
01:23:00,225 --> 01:23:02,769
even if we look like The Addams Family,
we're still like that.

1425
01:23:02,852 --> 01:23:04,854
♪♪

1426
01:23:06,523 --> 01:23:08,525
[Kourtney] <i>We balance each other.</i>

1427
01:23:08,608 --> 01:23:11,027
[♪ electric guitar playing]

1428
01:23:11,111 --> 01:23:14,864
<i>He's one of the hardest</i>
<i>working people that I know.</i>

1429
01:23:14,948 --> 01:23:17,701
{\an8}He's gonna go, and we're gonna
all make eye contact

1430
01:23:17,784 --> 01:23:19,285
{\an8}-for the stop, okay?
-Okay.

1431
01:23:19,369 --> 01:23:23,623
{\an8}[Kourtney] <i>He's really so dedicated</i>
<i>and passionate about his work.</i>

1432
01:23:24,374 --> 01:23:26,001
[announcer] [over speakers]
<i>Let's bring out the greatest drummers</i>

1433
01:23:26,084 --> 01:23:29,963
<i>of all time, Travis Barker of Blink-182.</i>

1434
01:23:30,046 --> 01:23:31,297
[crowd cheers]

1435
01:23:35,635 --> 01:23:38,763
Drumming is something I've done
since I was four years old.

1436
01:23:39,305 --> 01:23:41,182
<i>Like, I'm not stopping now.</i>

1437
01:23:43,893 --> 01:23:45,520
I'm not a person that can idle.

1438
01:23:45,603 --> 01:23:47,397
[crowd cheering]

1439
01:23:51,985 --> 01:23:54,446
<i>Whether it's designing a shoe for Vans</i>

1440
01:23:54,529 --> 01:23:56,364
<i>or playing with other artists,</i>

1441
01:23:57,365 --> 01:23:59,159
<i>you know, or producing,</i>

1442
01:23:59,868 --> 01:24:01,286
<i>I need challenges.</i>

1443
01:24:02,579 --> 01:24:03,913
<i>♪ Travie, where the drums at? ♪</i>

1444
01:24:03,997 --> 01:24:05,165
<i>♪ Uh... ♪</i>

1445
01:24:05,248 --> 01:24:07,751
[Lil Wayne] <i>To work in the studio</i>
<i>with Travis is interesting</i>

1446
01:24:07,834 --> 01:24:10,545
<i>because that's like</i>
<i>working with a producer</i>

1447
01:24:10,628 --> 01:24:13,798
that's gonna make the beat
right there in front of you.

1448
01:24:14,424 --> 01:24:16,718
<i>That's pretty rare these days.</i>

1449
01:24:17,385 --> 01:24:19,137
[Trippie Redd]
<i>Every time he gets on a song,</i>

1450
01:24:19,220 --> 01:24:21,765
{\an8}it's adding, like, some off-the-wall shit.

1451
01:24:21,848 --> 01:24:24,601
{\an8}It's not nothin' normal,
like, the way he plays.

1452
01:24:26,436 --> 01:24:28,438
[Lawrence]
<i>He's found himself now as an artist.</i>

1453
01:24:29,147 --> 01:24:31,066
<i>He's hit his stride as a producer.</i>

1454
01:24:31,149 --> 01:24:35,028
[♪ "bloody valentine"
by MGK and Travis Barker playing]

1455
01:24:37,030 --> 01:24:40,825
<i>♪ I don't do fake love,</i>
<i>but I'll take some from you tonight... ♪</i>

1456
01:24:40,909 --> 01:24:42,911
[MGK] <i>Travis is just an all-in guy.</i>

1457
01:24:43,620 --> 01:24:45,371
{\an8}The process never stopped.

1458
01:24:45,455 --> 01:24:48,458
<i>Like, we lived and breathed</i>
<i>the </i>Tickets to My Downfall <i>album.</i>

1459
01:24:49,084 --> 01:24:50,585
<i>♪ ...let's play pretend... ♪</i>

1460
01:24:50,668 --> 01:24:53,046
{\an8}It was just a huge inspiration
to see someone like Travis

1461
01:24:53,129 --> 01:24:54,756
{\an8}that excited about our band.

1462
01:24:55,840 --> 01:24:59,552
<i>A good producer finding in you</i>
<i>what you're capable of,</i>

1463
01:24:59,636 --> 01:25:00,970
<i>that's the job.</i>

1464
01:25:01,054 --> 01:25:03,932
{\an8}<i>♪ Na-na-na, na-na-na ♪</i>

1465
01:25:04,015 --> 01:25:05,016
{\an8}<i>♪ Na-na-na... ♪</i>

1466
01:25:05,100 --> 01:25:06,392
[MGK] <i>He's just here for the music.</i>

1467
01:25:07,102 --> 01:25:09,813
<i>He knows where it's going,</i>
<i>he's got a crazy vision.</i>

1468
01:25:09,896 --> 01:25:12,440
♪♪

1469
01:25:19,906 --> 01:25:22,367
{\an8}[Mark] <i>It takes three people</i>
<i>for Blink to work</i>

1470
01:25:23,368 --> 01:25:25,370
{\an8}<i>and the band was on indefinite hiatus.</i>

1471
01:25:26,830 --> 01:25:32,210
I hadn't really talked to Tom in years.
Like, we broke off everything.

1472
01:25:33,378 --> 01:25:38,049
<i>And then, one day, Tom texted me</i>
<i>a picture of a video that he was shooting.</i>

1473
01:25:38,133 --> 01:25:39,717
I texted back,
"That's awesome. Stoked for you.

1474
01:25:39,801 --> 01:25:42,554
Uh, by the way, I have cancer,
and I start chemotherapy."

1475
01:25:45,640 --> 01:25:47,851
<i>And immediately,</i>
<i>my phone rings and it's Tom.</i>

1476
01:25:49,185 --> 01:25:51,813
[Tom] <i>I was like, "Oh, my God.</i>
<i>I'm comin' up to see you."</i>

1477
01:25:51,896 --> 01:25:56,151
So, I drove up to see him,
and then Travis was there.

1478
01:25:57,986 --> 01:26:01,614
<i>It was a heavy conversation</i>
<i>because of what Mark was about to endure.</i>

1479
01:26:03,241 --> 01:26:05,660
[Travis] <i>He had stage 4A lymphoma.</i>

1480
01:26:07,162 --> 01:26:09,122
<i>I would go spend time</i>
<i>with Mark quite a bit.</i>

1481
01:26:09,873 --> 01:26:12,876
Tom had reached out.
He was also spendin' some time with Mark.

1482
01:26:14,335 --> 01:26:16,171
One of us was there almost every day.

1483
01:26:18,673 --> 01:26:21,509
{\an8}[Mark]<i> I was trying to be hopeful</i>
<i>through my chemotherapy</i>

1484
01:26:21,593 --> 01:26:22,969
{\an8}<i>and put on a brave face,</i>

1485
01:26:23,052 --> 01:26:25,388
but I was not so confident on the inside.

1486
01:26:26,681 --> 01:26:29,434
<i>I was despairing.</i>
<i>What was gonna happen?</i>

1487
01:26:30,560 --> 01:26:31,936
<i>Tomorrow, I have chemotherapy,</i>

1488
01:26:32,020 --> 01:26:33,354
<i>I'm gonna feel like hell the next day,</i>

1489
01:26:33,438 --> 01:26:34,647
<i>I'm gonna feel like hell the next day.</i>

1490
01:26:35,982 --> 01:26:38,651
We were just trying to give him
any kind of support,

1491
01:26:38,735 --> 01:26:40,028
do anything we could for him.

1492
01:26:42,071 --> 01:26:43,907
<i>And we had said during that time,</i>

1493
01:26:43,990 --> 01:26:46,784
<i>when Mark beats this,</i>
<i>we're gonna make music again.</i>

1494
01:26:46,868 --> 01:26:48,119
<i>We're gonna tour again.</i>

1495
01:26:50,455 --> 01:26:52,874
<i>And sure enough, Mark beat it.</i>

1496
01:26:53,917 --> 01:26:58,129
♪♪

1497
01:27:01,216 --> 01:27:04,844
[audience cheering]

1498
01:27:04,928 --> 01:27:07,055
[Mark] <i>We walk on stage,</i>
<i>and I didn't know what to expect.</i>

1499
01:27:07,138 --> 01:27:10,642
<i>I mean, Blink has been around,</i>
<i>at that point, for almost 30 years...</i>

1500
01:27:10,725 --> 01:27:13,394
[cheering continues]

1501
01:27:13,478 --> 01:27:14,687
<i>...and it's a packed house.</i>

1502
01:27:14,771 --> 01:27:17,857
<i>It's more people</i>
<i>than we played for in forever.</i>

1503
01:27:20,109 --> 01:27:21,653
<i>It felt like coming home.</i>

1504
01:27:23,488 --> 01:27:27,116
[cheering intensifies]

1505
01:27:27,200 --> 01:27:29,827
-[♪ "ONE MORE TIME" playing]
<i>-♪ Strangers ♪</i>

1506
01:27:29,911 --> 01:27:32,664
<i>♪ From strangers into brothers ♪</i>

1507
01:27:32,747 --> 01:27:37,293
<i>♪ From brothers</i>
<i>into strangers once again ♪</i>

1508
01:27:37,377 --> 01:27:39,879
<i>♪ We saw the whole world ♪</i>

1509
01:27:41,005 --> 01:27:43,591
<i>♪ But I couldn't see the meaning ♪</i>

1510
01:27:43,967 --> 01:27:47,887
<i>♪ I couldn't even recognize</i>
<i>my friends... ♪</i>

1511
01:27:47,971 --> 01:27:49,430
[Tom] <i>We got back together the first time</i>

1512
01:27:49,514 --> 01:27:50,723
<i>'cause Travis survived a plane crash.</i>

1513
01:27:50,807 --> 01:27:53,643
<i>I was like, "Holy shit.</i>
<i>If you can get through this, I'm here."</i>

1514
01:27:54,644 --> 01:27:56,062
And we broke up again.

1515
01:27:56,145 --> 01:27:58,106
After that, then Mark had cancer.

1516
01:27:58,189 --> 01:28:00,566
"Holy shit.
When you get through this, I'm here."

1517
01:28:00,650 --> 01:28:05,697
<i>♪ Do I have to die to hear you miss me? ♪</i>

1518
01:28:06,239 --> 01:28:11,286
<i>♪ Do I have to die</i>
<i>to hear you say goodbye? ♪</i>

1519
01:28:12,120 --> 01:28:17,333
<i>♪ I don't want to act</i>
<i>like there's tomorrow ♪</i>

1520
01:28:17,417 --> 01:28:22,964
<i>♪ I don't want to wait</i>
<i>to do this one more time ♪</i>

1521
01:28:23,047 --> 01:28:25,883
<i>♪ One more time... ♪</i>

1522
01:28:25,967 --> 01:28:27,885
[Tom] <i>This song came from Travis.</i>

1523
01:28:28,594 --> 01:28:31,597
<i>Putting forth a song</i>
<i>with such direct lyrics</i>

1524
01:28:31,681 --> 01:28:34,309
<i>is extremely expressive for Travis.</i>

1525
01:28:34,892 --> 01:28:36,477
<i>♪ I miss you ♪</i>

1526
01:28:37,603 --> 01:28:40,315
<i>♪ Took time, but I admit it ♪</i>

1527
01:28:40,398 --> 01:28:44,610
<i>♪ It still hurts</i>
<i>even after all these years... ♪</i>

1528
01:28:45,528 --> 01:28:48,364
[Travis] <i>Throughout the years</i>
<i>of grief and trauma</i>

1529
01:28:48,448 --> 01:28:51,576
<i>and trying to figure out</i>
<i>how and why everything happens...</i>

1530
01:28:52,910 --> 01:28:56,331
<i>what I learned,</i>
<i>life's just not for certain.</i>

1531
01:28:56,414 --> 01:29:01,919
<i>♪ I don't want to act like</i>
<i>there's tomorrow ♪</i>

1532
01:29:02,003 --> 01:29:07,800
<i>♪ I don't want to wait</i>
<i>to do this one more time ♪</i>

1533
01:29:07,884 --> 01:29:10,219
<i>♪ One more time ♪</i>

1534
01:29:10,303 --> 01:29:13,222
<i>♪ One more time ♪</i>

1535
01:29:13,806 --> 01:29:15,725
<i>♪ I miss you ♪</i>

1536
01:29:15,808 --> 01:29:17,435
[audience cheering]

1537
01:29:17,518 --> 01:29:18,644
[Mark] We're Blink-182.

1538
01:29:18,728 --> 01:29:20,688
Thank you all so very much
for being with us tonight.

1539
01:29:20,772 --> 01:29:22,106
We love you!

1540
01:29:25,651 --> 01:29:29,072
[cheering continues, fades]

1541
01:29:32,325 --> 01:29:33,743
[Travis] <i>Every day I open my eyes,</i>

1542
01:29:33,826 --> 01:29:36,537
<i>I'm reminded of walking away</i>
<i>from a plane crash</i>

1543
01:29:36,621 --> 01:29:38,039
<i>where four people passed away.</i>

1544
01:29:38,873 --> 01:29:40,750
[♪ gentle music playing]

1545
01:29:40,833 --> 01:29:43,836
<i>And then, AM passing away,</i>
<i>like, less than a year later.</i>

1546
01:29:45,838 --> 01:29:49,467
But I've also accepted who I am now and...

1547
01:29:52,887 --> 01:29:54,305
[clicks tongue]

1548
01:30:14,826 --> 01:30:17,078
[sighs, sniffles]

1549
01:30:17,787 --> 01:30:20,748
♪♪

1550
01:30:21,833 --> 01:30:22,834
[sniffles]

1551
01:30:26,087 --> 01:30:27,839
I think I've, you know...

1552
01:30:30,258 --> 01:30:31,426
[exhales sharply]

1553
01:30:33,636 --> 01:30:37,849
<i>I've figured out a way to carry on</i>
<i>and live my best in their memory.</i>

1554
01:30:41,727 --> 01:30:43,146
[Linda] <i>It's always hard...</i>

1555
01:30:44,605 --> 01:30:46,524
because the "what if" is there,

1556
01:30:47,525 --> 01:30:50,278
and the "what ifs" can kill your life.

1557
01:30:50,361 --> 01:30:52,947
♪♪

1558
01:30:53,030 --> 01:30:57,160
<i>So, I let him know</i>
<i>there's no hard feelings here.</i>

1559
01:31:00,288 --> 01:31:02,623
[Travis]
<i>It took years of survivor's guilt...</i>

1560
01:31:04,083 --> 01:31:07,295
<i>of trying to understand</i>
<i>what they'd want me to do.</i>

1561
01:31:08,588 --> 01:31:10,423
[crying] And I've felt like
never flying again

1562
01:31:10,506 --> 01:31:12,175
would probably...

1563
01:31:12,258 --> 01:31:13,342
[sniffles]

1564
01:31:15,094 --> 01:31:17,096
...not be one of those things, you know?

1565
01:31:21,225 --> 01:31:24,061
{\an8}[speed bag thudding]

1566
01:31:25,855 --> 01:31:28,357
{\an8}<i>When I first started</i>
<i>thinking about flying again,</i>

1567
01:31:28,441 --> 01:31:31,319
I actually had a series of...

1568
01:31:31,402 --> 01:31:32,695
There was, like, nightmares.

1569
01:31:32,778 --> 01:31:35,156
'Cause for so long,
it didn't even enter my head.

1570
01:31:38,451 --> 01:31:42,288
[Kourtney] <i>I could never truly understand</i>
<i>what he went through</i>

1571
01:31:42,371 --> 01:31:44,999
<i>or what he still feels to this day.</i>

1572
01:31:46,501 --> 01:31:50,171
<i>So, I was like,</i>
<i>"You never have to fly again.</i>

1573
01:31:50,254 --> 01:31:52,465
<i>I would never be mad at you for that."</i>

1574
01:31:54,634 --> 01:31:57,637
For our first Valentine's Day together,

1575
01:31:58,513 --> 01:32:01,599
<i>I made him this collage of a tour bus</i>

1576
01:32:01,682 --> 01:32:05,895
<i>and all these different places</i>
<i>that I'd love to drive to with him.</i>

1577
01:32:07,647 --> 01:32:11,192
[Travis] <i>But I had this force</i>
<i>within me that was like,</i>

1578
01:32:11,275 --> 01:32:14,237
<i>"I don't wanna be restricted</i>
<i>by anything anymore.</i>

1579
01:32:15,238 --> 01:32:18,407
There's nothing that's
gonna have power over me."

1580
01:32:18,491 --> 01:32:21,118
[♪ intense music playing]

1581
01:32:22,787 --> 01:32:26,457
[Kourtney] <i>Eventually, he said to me,</i>
<i>"If you plan a trip</i>

1582
01:32:26,541 --> 01:32:30,628
<i>and it's somewhere that</i>
<i>I couldn't drive to, I'll go."</i>

1583
01:32:32,797 --> 01:32:34,590
<i>But he didn't wanna know about it</i>

1584
01:32:34,674 --> 01:32:37,885
until 24 hours before the flight,

1585
01:32:37,969 --> 01:32:41,931
<i>so he didn't have too much time</i>
<i>to think about it.</i>

1586
01:32:45,601 --> 01:32:50,106
{\an8}When he came to tell us kids,
we were really against it at first

1587
01:32:50,189 --> 01:32:51,941
{\an8}'cause all we had known is "no."

1588
01:32:52,024 --> 01:32:54,569
"No flying." "Don't fly." "Let's not fly."

1589
01:32:54,652 --> 01:32:56,862
{\an8}He told us, he was like,
"Yeah, I'm gonna get on a plane."

1590
01:32:56,946 --> 01:32:58,573
{\an8}And we were like,
"Fuck, no, you're not." [chuckles]

1591
01:32:58,656 --> 01:33:00,491
{\an8}You're like--
'Cause that's all we knew growing up

1592
01:33:00,575 --> 01:33:02,618
{\an8}was we're never getting on a plane.

1593
01:33:05,371 --> 01:33:09,000
I think I inherited paranoia
[slight chuckle] from him.

1594
01:33:10,835 --> 01:33:13,087
<i>My little sister's</i>
<i>really bad with it</i>, <i>too.</i>

1595
01:33:13,963 --> 01:33:16,966
<i>♪♪</i>

1596
01:33:18,092 --> 01:33:20,720
[Kourtney] <i>When I told him that,</i>

1597
01:33:20,803 --> 01:33:26,225
<i>"I have a flight booked,</i>
<i>we're going to Mexico,"</i>

1598
01:33:26,309 --> 01:33:30,271
he took it in and was like, "Okay."

1599
01:33:31,772 --> 01:33:36,611
<i>He started getting more anxious</i>
<i>as the day went on.</i>

1600
01:33:37,361 --> 01:33:39,447
<i>So we did breath work.</i>

1601
01:33:39,530 --> 01:33:43,784
<i>And then, this just sounds crazy,</i>
<i>but during my breath work,</i>

1602
01:33:43,868 --> 01:33:48,122
<i>a vision of his mom came to me</i>
<i>and was like,</i>

1603
01:33:48,205 --> 01:33:51,042
<i>"Thank you for taking care of my son."</i>

1604
01:33:52,043 --> 01:33:54,920
[♪ "To Build a Home"
by The Cinematic Orchestra playing]

1605
01:34:05,556 --> 01:34:08,392
<i>We drove to the airport in the morning.</i>

1606
01:34:10,353 --> 01:34:12,605
I remember him calling his dad.

1607
01:34:14,023 --> 01:34:18,527
<i>♪ There is a house built out of stone... ♪</i>

1608
01:34:18,611 --> 01:34:19,862
[Travis] Hey, Pal.

1609
01:34:19,945 --> 01:34:21,197
[Randy] [over phone] <i>Yeah?</i>

1610
01:34:21,822 --> 01:34:25,451
[Travis] <i>I had all sorts of emotions</i>
<i>driving to the airport.</i>

1611
01:34:27,036 --> 01:34:29,955
My kids were saying, "Don't do it, Dad.
Like, you don't have to do it."

1612
01:34:30,831 --> 01:34:35,544
<i>♪ Tables and chairs</i>
<i>worn by all of the dust... ♪</i>

1613
01:34:35,628 --> 01:34:38,297
<i>My kids were carrying my trauma.</i>

1614
01:34:49,850 --> 01:34:52,311
[Travis] <i>I just knew, if I can do this,</i>

1615
01:34:52,395 --> 01:34:55,690
<i>I could not only do it for myself,</i>
<i>but also do it for my children,</i>

1616
01:34:56,232 --> 01:34:58,567
and they could overcome it.

1617
01:34:58,651 --> 01:35:01,404
[engine rumbling]

1618
01:35:02,279 --> 01:35:05,282
♪♪

1619
01:35:11,414 --> 01:35:14,208
<i>Love makes you do crazy things.</i>

1620
01:35:14,667 --> 01:35:19,004
<i>♪ And I built ♪</i>

1621
01:35:20,923 --> 01:35:22,174
<i>♪ A home... ♪</i>

1622
01:35:22,258 --> 01:35:25,219
<i>It puts you back in places</i>
<i>you swore you'd never go again.</i>

1623
01:35:27,596 --> 01:35:29,765
<i>♪ For me... ♪</i>

1624
01:35:29,849 --> 01:35:33,894
<i>It makes you risk your pride,</i>
<i>your comfort,</i>

1625
01:35:34,729 --> 01:35:37,523
<i>and the walls you spent years</i>
<i>building up around you.</i>

1626
01:35:40,109 --> 01:35:41,944
<i>♪ For me... ♪</i>

1627
01:35:42,611 --> 01:35:45,948
<i>Love is louder than fear.</i>

1628
01:35:47,324 --> 01:35:51,620
<i>♪ And now, it's time ♪</i>

1629
01:35:53,372 --> 01:35:58,711
<i>♪ To leave ♪</i>

